(
  'butter-chicken-murgh-makhani',
  'butter-chicken-murgh-makhani',
  'Old Delhi Style Murgh Makhani (Butter Chicken)',
  'Velvety fenugreek & tomato sauce with smoky charred tandoori chicken',
  'A masterpiece of North Indian cuisine. Marinated chicken thighs are charred under high heat, then simmered in a silken reduction of vine-ripened tomatoes, cashew cream, butter, and fragrant dried fenugreek leaves (kasoori methi).',
  'Indian',
  'North Indian / Punjabi',
  '25 mins',
  25,
  '35 mins',
  35,
  '60 mins',
  4,
  'Medium',
  4.95,
  342,
  580,
  '"Signature","Gluten-Free","Rich & Creamy","Crowd Favorite","North Indian / Punjabi","Indian","High-Protein","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Heavy-bottom Dutch oven or cast iron pot","Immersion blender or high-speed blender","Grill pan or broiler tray","Fine mesh sieve","Mixing bowls"',
  '[{"name":"Boneless chicken thighs, cut into bite-sized pieces","amount":750,"unit":"g","notes":"Pat dry before marinating","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Full-fat Greek yogurt","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Thick / strained","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Ginger-garlic paste","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Freshly made 1:1 ginger and garlic","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Kashmiri red chili powder","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Vibrant red color without extreme heat","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Garam masala","amount":1.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Freshly ground","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Ground cumin","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Toasted","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Ripe Roma tomatoes, roughly chopped","amount":800,"unit":"g","notes":"Sweet, deep red tomatoes","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Raw cashews","amount":0.25,"unit":"cup","notes":"Soaked in warm water for 15 mins","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Salted butter (cold cubes)","amount":60,"unit":"g","notes":"Divided","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Heavy whipping cream","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"At room temperature","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Kasoori Methi (dried fenugreek leaves)","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Lightly crushed between palms","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Honey or brown sugar","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"To balance tomato acidity","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Green cardamom pods","amount":4,"unit":"whole","notes":"Lightly bruised","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Kosher salt","amount":1.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"To taste","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"First & Second Marinade","instruction":"Coat chicken with 1 tbsp ginger-garlic paste, 1 tbsp Kashmiri chili, 1 tsp salt, and juice of 1 lime. Let sit for 15 mins. Stir in Greek yogurt, 1 tsp garam masala, and 1 tbsp mustard oil. Marinate refrigerated for at least 1 hour (preferably overnight).","time":"15 mins + chill","temp":"Refrigerated (38°F / 3°C)","visualCue":"The chicken will look glossy, richly crimson, and evenly coated in thick yogurt marinade."},{"step":2,"title":"Char the Chicken","instruction":"Preheat oven broiler or a smoking-hot cast-iron grill pan. Thread chicken onto skewers or arrange on wire rack. Cook on high heat for 6-8 mins each side until deeply charred with smoky spots, but only 85% cooked through.","time":"12-14 mins","temp":"500°F (260°C) / Broil High","visualCue":"Edges should develop deep mahogany blisters and aroma of tandoor smoke."},{"step":3,"title":"Simmer the Tomato-Cashew Gravy","instruction":"In a Dutch oven, melt 20g butter. Add cardamom pods, remaining ginger-garlic paste, chopped tomatoes, soaked cashews, 1 cup water, and 1 tsp chili powder. Simmer uncovered for 20 minutes until tomatoes completely break down into mush.","time":"20 mins","temp":"Medium-low heat","visualCue":"Tomatoes will lose their raw pungency, and liquid will reduce by half."},{"step":4,"title":"Blend & Strain to Silk","instruction":"Remove whole cardamoms. Transfer tomato mixture to a high-speed blender and puree until ultra-smooth. Strain through a fine-mesh sieve back into the pot, pressing with a ladle.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"The sauce must flow like warm velvet with no seed or skin texture remaining."},{"step":5,"title":"Finish with Cream, Butter & Fenugreek","instruction":"Return gravy to a gentle simmer. Whisk in honey, remaining cold cubed butter, and heavy cream. Add charred chicken pieces and simmer gently for 6-8 mins. Crush kasoori methi between palms and sprinkle on top with a pinch of garam masala. Rest 5 mins before serving with garlic naan.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Low simmer (180°F / 82°C)","visualCue":"Sauce turns a lush sunset orange; shimmering dots of spiced butter pool on the surface."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Always strain the tomato sauce through a fine-mesh sieve — this is the secret to restaurant-grade velvety texture.","Rubbing kasoori methi between warm palms releases essential aromatic oils right as it hits the hot curry.","Do not boil heavily after adding heavy cream; a gentle simmer prevents dairy separation."',
  '[{"original":"Chicken thighs","alternative":"Paneer cubes or firm tofu","notes":"Pan-fry paneer cubes till golden before simmering."},{"original":"Heavy cream","alternative":"Full-fat coconut cream","notes":"Provides luscious creaminess with subtle tropical note."},{"original":"Kashmiri chili","alternative":"Sweet paprika + 1/4 tsp cayenne","notes":"Matches vibrant red tone without blistering heat."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Skipping the straining step","remedy":"Leaves tomato seeds and cashew grit, ruining the trademark makhani mouthfeel."},{"mistake":"Overcooking the chicken during charring","remedy":"Take it off the grill when slightly underdone; it finishes cooking gently in the gravy."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy","Tree Nuts (Cashews)"',
  'Ensure internal temperature of chicken pieces reaches 165°F (74°C) during the simmer.',
  'Keeps remarkably well! Flavors deepen after 24 hours. Store in airtight container in fridge up to 4 days, or freeze up to 2 months.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1603894584373-5ac82b2ae398?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~466g)","calories":580,"energyKj":2427,"protein":41,"carbohydrates":35,"sugar":5,"fiber":5,"totalFat":22,"saturatedFat":8,"sodium":812}'::jsonb
),
(
  'classic-bolognese-ragu',
  'classic-bolognese-ragu',
  'Slow-Braised Tagliatelle al Ragù Bolognese',
  'Slow-cooked milk and white wine ragù over silk handmade ribbon pasta',
  'The true authentic recipe from Bologna, Italy. A fine mirepoix sautéed gently with ground beef chuck, pancetta, and pork, deglazed with dry Italian white wine, then slowly braised in whole milk and San Marzano tomatoes for four hours until meltingly tender.',
  'Italian',
  'Italian (Emilia-Romagna)',
  '25 mins',
  25,
  '120 mins',
  120,
  '145 mins',
  6,
  'Medium',
  4.98,
  420,
  640,
  '"Classic","Slow Food","Comfort Food","Sunday Dinner","Italian (Emilia-Romagna)","Italian","Vegetarian","Nut-Free"',
  '"Enameled cast-iron Dutch oven","Large pasta pot","Wooden spoon","Chef's knife and cutting board","Box grater"',
  '[{"name":"Pancetta or unsmoked bacon, finely minced","amount":100,"unit":"g","notes":"Rendered slowly for savory fat base","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Coarsely ground beef chuck (80/20)","amount":500,"unit":"g","notes":"Best flavor and moisture","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Ground pork shoulder","amount":250,"unit":"g","notes":"Adds tenderness","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Yellow onion, finely minced","amount":1,"unit":"medium","notes":"Brunoise cut","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Carrot, peeled and finely minced","amount":1,"unit":"medium","notes":"Brunoise cut","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Celery stalk, finely minced","amount":1,"unit":"stalk","notes":"Brunoise cut","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Dry Italian white wine (Trebbiano or Pinot Grigio)","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Room temp","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Whole milk","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Tenderizes meat fibers","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"San Marzano canned whole tomatoes, hand-crushed","amount":400,"unit":"g","notes":"Authentic Italian ragù uses minimal tomato","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh bay leaf","amount":2,"unit":"leaves","notes":"Aromatic backbone","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Freshly grated nutmeg","amount":0.25,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Crucial Bolognese aroma","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Fresh egg tagliatelle pasta","amount":500,"unit":"g","notes":"Wide flat ribbons grip the sauce","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Parmigiano-Reggiano, freshly microplaned","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"24-month aged","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Unsalted butter","amount":30,"unit":"g","notes":"To emulsify pasta in pan","category":"Dairy"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Render the Pancetta & Soffritto","instruction":"Heat your Dutch oven over medium-low. Add minced pancetta and render until fat is released and bits turn lightly crisp (8 mins). Add minced onion, carrot, and celery. Cook gently for 12-15 minutes until vegetables are translucent and sweet without browning.","time":"15 mins","temp":"Medium-low heat","visualCue":"Mirepoix softens completely and releases an intoxicating herbal sweetness."},{"step":2,"title":"Brown the Meats Gently","instruction":"Raise heat to medium. Add ground beef and pork. Break up gently with wooden spoon. Cook until no pink remains, but do not sear into crunchy crumbles — keep meat tender and juicy.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Meat should be pale and fragrant, releasing natural juices."},{"step":3,"title":"Deglaze with White Wine","instruction":"Pour in the dry white wine. Scrape the fond from the bottom of the Dutch oven. Simmer briskly until the wine has almost completely evaporated and the alcohol smell is gone.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"The pan bottom becomes clean and the aroma transforms from boozy to deeply savory."},{"step":4,"title":"The Milk Braise & Tomato Simmer","instruction":"Pour in the whole milk and grate fresh nutmeg. Bring to a bare bubble, then add the hand-crushed San Marzano tomatoes, bay leaves, 1 tsp salt, and cracked black pepper. Reduce heat to absolute lowest setting, cover with lid slightly ajar, and braise for 2 to 3 hours, stirring every 20 minutes and adding a splash of water if dry.","time":"120 mins","temp":"Bare whisper simmer (185°F / 85°C)","visualCue":"The sauce thickens to an amber-hued glossy ragù; droplets of rich orange fat rise to the edge."},{"step":5,"title":"Mantecatura with Fresh Tagliatelle","instruction":"Cook fresh tagliatelle in salted boiling water for 2-3 mins until al dente. Reserve 1/2 cup pasta cooking water. Transfer pasta directly into the ragù pan with 30g butter and a splash of pasta water. Toss vigorously for 1 minute off the heat, then shower with Parmigiano-Reggiano.","time":"4 mins","temp":"Boiling water / Pan toss","visualCue":"Every ribbon of tagliatelle is coated in a velvety, clinging glaze of ragù."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Authentic Bolognese uses dry WHITE wine, not red. White wine preserves the delicate sweetness of the milk and veal/pork.","The milk tenderizes the meats via lactic acid, creating melt-in-your-mouth tenderness instead of chewy granules.","Never serve ragù with skinny spaghetti; ribbons like tagliatelle or pappardelle hold the hefty meat sauce."',
  '[{"original":"Ground pork","alternative":"Ground veal or extra ground chuck","notes":"Keep fat content around 20%."},{"original":"Tagliatelle","alternative":"Pappardelle or rigatoni","notes":"Tubular shapes also catch ragù well."},{"original":"Pancetta","alternative":"Prosciutto ends or unsmoked thick-cut bacon","notes":"Render thoroughly."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Adding too much tomato sauce","remedy":"Ragù is a braised meat dish lightly stained with tomato, not a marinara."},{"mistake":"Hard boiling the sauce","remedy":"Boiling curdles milk and dries out meat fibers; keep it at a lazy, occasional blip."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy","Gluten","Eggs"',
  'Store leftover ragù promptly in refrigerator; do not leave at room temperature for over 2 hours.',
  'Refrigerate up to 5 days, or freeze in portions for up to 3 months. In fact, day two is even more delicious!',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1598866594230-a7c12756260f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~508g)","calories":640,"energyKj":2678,"protein":22,"carbohydrates":70,"sugar":8,"fiber":10,"totalFat":22,"saturatedFat":7,"sodium":768}'::jsonb
),
(
  'crispy-chili-crisp-dumplings',
  'crispy-chili-crisp-dumplings',
  'Lace-Crusted Vegetable & Shiitake Dumplings',
  'Golden webbed crispy bottom with juicy ginger-scallion filling & homemade chili crisp',
  'Hand-pleated potstickers packed with umami-rich sautéed shiitake mushrooms, shredded napa cabbage, charred scallions, and fresh water chestnuts. Cooked using the authentic cornstarch slurry technique for an irresistible, restaurant-style crispy lace skirt.',
  'Asian',
  'Chinese / Cantonese',
  '30 mins',
  30,
  '15 mins',
  15,
  '45 mins',
  4,
  'Medium',
  4.88,
  215,
  360,
  '"Vegetarian","Crispy","Street Food","Umami Bomb","Chinese / Cantonese","Chinese","Snack","Asian","Vegan","Dairy-Free","Nut-Free","Low-Sugar"',
  '"10 or 12-inch non-stick skillet with tight-fitting lid","Large mixing bowl","Clean kitchen towel or cheesecloth","Small whisk"',
  '[{"name":"Round dumpling wrappers (potsticker skins)","amount":28,"unit":"wrappers","notes":"Fresh or thawed","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh shiitake mushrooms, finely diced","amount":200,"unit":"g","notes":"Stems discarded or saved for broth","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Napa cabbage, finely shredded","amount":3,"unit":"cups","notes":"Salted and squeezed completely dry","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Scallions (green onions), finely sliced","amount":4,"unit":"stalks","notes":"Whites and greens separated","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh ginger, finely grated","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Grated on microplane","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Garlic cloves, minced","amount":3,"unit":"cloves","notes":"Very finely minced","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Water chestnuts, finely minced","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"For signature crisp texture","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Toasted sesame oil","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Aromatic oil","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Low-sodium soy sauce","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Umami base","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Vegetarian mushroom oyster sauce","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Deep savory glaze","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Cornstarch (for lace slurry)","amount":1.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Whisked with 1/3 cup cold water","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Neutral vegetable oil","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Avocado or peanut oil for frying","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Chili crisp oil + black vinegar","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For serving dipping sauce","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Squeeze Cabbage & Prep Filling","instruction":"Toss shredded napa cabbage with 1/2 tsp salt in a bowl. Let sit 10 mins, then bundle in a clean tea towel and squeeze forcefully over the sink to extract all excess water. This prevents soggy dumplings.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Cabbage should reduce to 1/3 volume and feel dry to the touch."},{"step":2,"title":"Mix the Savory Umami Filling","instruction":"In a large bowl, combine squeezed cabbage, diced shiitakes, scallions, grated ginger, minced garlic, water chestnuts, sesame oil, soy sauce, mushroom oyster sauce, 1/2 tsp white pepper, and 1 tsp cornstarch. Stir vigorously in one direction until cohesive.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Mixture binds together lightly without excess pooling liquid."},{"step":3,"title":"Pleat the Dumplings","instruction":"Place 1 tbsp filling into center of each wrapper. Moisten rim with cold water. Fold in half, creating 3-4 pleats along the top edge while pressing out air bubbles, and seal tightly. Tap bottom flat on cutting board.","time":"15 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Dumplings sit upright like plump crescents with a flat bottom."},{"step":4,"title":"Sear & Steam with Lace Slurry","instruction":"Heat 1 tbsp oil in a non-stick skillet over medium-high. Arrange dumplings in a circular pinwheel. Fry undisturbed for 2-3 mins until bottoms are golden. Whisk together 1/3 cup water, 1.5 tsp cornstarch, and 1 tsp vinegar; pour directly into the pan. Cover immediately with lid.","time":"6 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"Loud vigorous sizzling and steam plumes fill the lid."},{"step":5,"title":"Form the Golden Lace Skirt","instruction":"Remove lid. Lower heat to medium and let remaining moisture evaporate. Drizzle 1 tsp oil around pan perimeter. Cook undisturbed until the cornstarch layer crisps into an amber, lattice-patterned web. Invert onto a serving plate and serve with spicy chili crisp dip.","time":"4 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Lattice peels gently away from pan edges, golden brown and shatteringly crisp."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Squeezing every drop of water from the salted cabbage is non-negotiable for tender, juicy dumpling interiors.","The teaspoon of vinegar in the cornstarch slurry helps achieve ultra-crisp, delicate lacy webs.","Always cover the dumplings with a damp towel while pleating to prevent wrappers from drying out."',
  '[{"original":"Shiitake mushrooms","alternative":"Ground chicken, pork, or firm crumbled tofu","notes":"If using meat, cook 2 mins longer."},{"original":"Water chestnuts","alternative":"Finely diced jicama or celery","notes":"Maintains crunchy freshness."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Trapping air inside dumplings","remedy":"Air bubbles expand during steaming and burst the seal."},{"mistake":"Lifting dumplings before the lace is dry","remedy":"Wait until all bubbles cease and the lace pulls away on its own."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten (wrappers)","Soy","Sesame"',
  'Careful when pouring water slurry into hot oiled skillet — it will splatter momentarily.',
  'Freeze un-cooked dumplings on a parchment sheet for 2 hours, then transfer to ziploc bags. Cook straight from frozen!',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1541696432-82c6da8ce7bf?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~312g)","calories":360,"energyKj":1506,"protein":13,"carbohydrates":40,"sugar":5,"fiber":5,"totalFat":13,"saturatedFat":4,"sodium":432}'::jsonb
),
(
  'belgian-chocolate-lava-cakes',
  'belgian-chocolate-lava-cakes',
  'Warm Valrhona Molten Dark Chocolate Lava Cakes',
  'Crackling baked crust with an intoxicating liquid ganache core & flaked sea salt',
  'The ultimate dessert decadence. High-percentage dark chocolate melted with European cultured butter and whipped farm eggs, baked to perfection so the perimeter forms an ethereal soufflé cake while the molten core cascades out warm upon the first spoonful.',
  'Desserts',
  'French Patisserie',
  '15 mins',
  15,
  '10 mins',
  10,
  '25 mins',
  4,
  'Easy',
  4.97,
  388,
  490,
  '"Decadent","Quick Gourmet","Vegetarian","Date Night","French Patisserie","French","Dessert","Desserts","Eggetarian","Nut-Free"',
  '"Four 6-ounce ceramic ramekins","Double boiler or heatproof glass bowl over saucepan","Hand mixer or wire whisk","Rubber spatula","Baking sheet"',
  '[{"name":"70% bittersweet dark chocolate (feves or chopped)","amount":170,"unit":"g","notes":"Valrhona, Guittard, or Callebaut","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Unsalted European butter","amount":115,"unit":"g","notes":"1 stick, cubed","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Powdered sugar (confectioners'')","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Sifted","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Whole large eggs (room temp)","amount":2,"unit":"whole","notes":"Fresh organic eggs","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Egg yolks (room temp)","amount":2,"unit":"yolks","notes":"For ultra-rich runny center","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Pure vanilla bean extract","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Rich vanilla notes","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Espresso powder","amount":0.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Enhances chocolate depth without tasting like coffee","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"All-purpose flour","amount":6,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Sifted","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Unsweetened Dutch cocoa powder","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For dusting ramekins","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Maldon flaky sea salt","amount":0.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"For finishing garnish","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Fresh raspberries & mint sprigs","amount":1,"unit":"handful","notes":"For plating contrast","category":"Produce"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Prep Ramekins & Oven","instruction":"Preheat oven to 425°F (220°C). Generously butter four 6-ounce ramekins with softened butter using upward brush strokes. Dust interior with cocoa powder, tapping out any loose excess.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Preheat 425°F (220°C)","visualCue":"Ramekins have an even, velvety cocoa coating on all walls and base."},{"step":2,"title":"Gently Melt Chocolate & Butter","instruction":"Place chopped dark chocolate and cubed butter in a heatproof bowl set over a pot of barely simmering water (double boiler). Stir gently with spatula until completely glossy and melted. Stir in espresso powder. Remove from heat and cool for 4 minutes.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Indirect steam","visualCue":"Lustrous, liquid silk with no lumps."},{"step":3,"title":"Whisk Eggs & Sugar","instruction":"In a separate bowl, whisk together whole eggs, egg yolks, powdered sugar, and vanilla extract until pale, slightly thickened, and ribbony (about 2 minutes with hand whisk).","time":"3 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Mixture turns creamy light yellow and forms soft ribbons."},{"step":4,"title":"Fold & Fill","instruction":"Pour the warm melted chocolate into the egg mixture. Gently fold with a rubber spatula. Sift in the flour and fold just until no dry streaks remain — do not overmix. Divide batter evenly among the 4 prepared ramekins.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Batter is thick, glossy, and mousse-like."},{"step":5,"title":"Precision Bake & Unmold","instruction":"Bake on center rack at 425°F for exactly 11 to 12 minutes. The tops should be set and matte with slightly cracked edges, but the center will jiggle softly when nudged. Rest for 1 minute. Run a thin knife around edges, place dessert plate over top, invert, and gently lift ramekin. Finish with flaky Maldon salt.","time":"11-12 mins","temp":"425°F (220°C)","visualCue":"Edges are firm cake; center has a soft, hypnotic wobble."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Never open the oven door during the first 8 minutes of baking to prevent temperature drops.","Using cocoa powder instead of flour to dust the ramekins ensures clean unmolding and leaves zero white flour residue.","The extra 2 egg yolks are the secret: egg whites set solid when heated, but yolks stay luscious and liquid!"',
  '[{"original":"All-purpose flour","alternative":"1:1 Gluten-free baking blend or almond flour","notes":"Gluten-free version works wonderfully."},{"original":"Powdered sugar","alternative":"Fine caster sugar","notes":"Powdered sugar dissolves faster for smoother batter."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Baking for just 2 minutes too long","remedy":"Turns into regular chocolate cake with no molten lava center. Use a timer!"},{"mistake":"Unmolding immediately straight out of oven","remedy":"Wait 60-90 seconds for edges to stabilize, otherwise the cake will collapse."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Eggs","Dairy","Gluten"',
  'Ramekins will be scorching hot; use heat-resistant silicone oven mitts when inverting.',
  'Best served immediately. Unbaked batter in ramekins can be refrigerated covered for up to 24 hours (add 2 minutes bake time).',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1606313564200-e75d5e30476c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~403g)","calories":490,"energyKj":2050,"protein":12,"carbohydrates":64,"sugar":48,"fiber":4,"totalFat":22,"saturatedFat":13,"sodium":172}'::jsonb
),
