  '"Brunch Favorite","Vegetarian","Fluffy","Citrus Bliss","Modern Brunch / American","Breakfast","Eggetarian","Nut-Free"',
  '"Large cast iron griddle or non-stick skillet","Two large mixing bowls","Hand mixer or balloon whisk","Microplane zester","Silicone spatula"',
  '[{"name":"Fresh whole milk ricotta cheese","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Drained on paper towels for 10 mins","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Large eggs (separated)","amount":3,"unit":"eggs","notes":"Yolks and whites in separate bowls","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Unbleached all-purpose flour","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Fluffed and leveled","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Whole milk or buttermilk","amount":0.75,"unit":"cup","notes":"Room temp","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Fresh Meyer lemon zest","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Finely microplaned","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh lemon juice","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Freshly squeezed","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Granulated cane sugar","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Divided","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Baking powder","amount":1.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Double acting","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Pure vanilla bean paste","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Fragrant aromatic","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Kosher salt","amount":0.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Balances sweetness","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Unsalted butter (for cooking)","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"To sizzle in pan","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Fresh blueberries or blackberries","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Tossed with 1 tsp maple syrup","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Pure grade A amber maple syrup","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Warmed for serving","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Lemon Sugar & Wet Base","instruction":"In a large bowl, rub lemon zest into granulated sugar with your fingertips until moist and fragrant like citrus sunshine. Whisk in ricotta, egg yolks, milk, lemon juice, and vanilla until smooth and creamy.","time":"4 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"A fragrant, pale cream batter base dotted with yellow lemon speckles."},{"step":2,"title":"Whisk Dry Ingredients","instruction":"Sift flour, baking powder, and salt into the ricotta mixture. Stir with a spatula just until barely incorporated (small lumps are totally fine). Do not overwork.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Thick, gently lumpy batter."},{"step":3,"title":"Whip Whites to Soft Peaks","instruction":"In a squeaky-clean bowl, whip egg whites with a pinch of salt until soft, glossy peaks form when beaters are lifted.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Whites resemble fluffy marshmallow clouds that hold their tip gently."},{"step":4,"title":"Fold with Cloud-Like Care","instruction":"Fold one-third of whipped egg whites into batter to lighten it. Gently fold in remaining egg whites in two batches using slow sweeping figure-eight motions with spatula.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Batter billows like light mousse and feels airy in the bowl."},{"step":5,"title":"Griddle to Golden Perfection","instruction":"Heat skillet over medium-low heat and melt 1 tbsp butter. Drop 1/3-cup mounds of batter. Cook gently for 3-4 minutes until bubbles emerge on surface and underside is rich golden brown. Flip delicately and cook 2-3 more minutes. Serve immediately topped with warm berries and real maple syrup.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium-low (325°F / 165°C)","visualCue":"Pancakes puff dramatically to nearly 1 inch high with golden filigree edges."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Rubbing lemon zest into the sugar first releases all the natural citrus oils via friction.","Whipping egg whites separately is the technique borrowed from Japanese soufflé pancakes that makes them float.","Cook on medium-low heat; high heat burns the exterior before the ricotta center cooks through."',
  '[{"original":"Ricotta cheese","alternative":"Cottage cheese (blended smooth) or mascarpone","notes":"Mascarpone adds even richer buttery body."},{"original":"All-purpose flour","alternative":"1:1 Gluten-free flour blend","notes":"Be extra gentle when folding."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Overmixing after folding egg whites","remedy":"Deflates air bubbles, yielding flat, dense pancakes instead of fluffy clouds."},{"mistake":"Flipping too early","remedy":"Wait until tiny air craters stay open on top before sliding the spatula underneath."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy","Eggs","Gluten"',
  'Keep griddle temperature moderate to avoid butter smoking and burning.',
  'Pancakes are best eaten fresh. Reheat leftovers in a 300°F oven for 5 minutes (never microwave).',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1528207776546-365bb710ee93?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~326g)","calories":380,"energyKj":1590,"protein":10,"carbohydrates":49,"sugar":37,"fiber":3,"totalFat":17,"saturatedFat":10,"sodium":133}'::jsonb
),
(
  'wild-mushroom-garlic-risotto',
  'wild-mushroom-garlic-risotto',
  'Creamy Roasted Garlic & Wild Forest Mushroom Risotto',
  'Arborio rice cooked slow with wine, thyme, Parmigiano-Reggiano & pan-seared oyster mushrooms',
  'A quintessential northern Italian comfort classic. Plump Carnaroli or Arborio rice toasted in fragrant shallot oil, deglazed with dry white wine, and slowly infused with hot vegetable broth until creamy and fluid (''all''onda''), finished with caramelized wild mushrooms and herb butter.',
  'Italian',
  'Northern Italian (Piedmont)',
  '15 mins',
  15,
  '30 mins',
  30,
  '45 mins',
  4,
  'Medium',
  4.92,
  164,
  450,
  '"Vegetarian","Cozy","Gluten-Free","Date Night Classic","Northern Italian (Piedmont)","Italian","Nut-Free"',
  '"Wide, heavy sauté pan or saucier","Medium saucepan (for broth)","Cast iron skillet (for searing mushrooms)","Wooden risotto spoon with hole","Ladle"',
  '[{"name":"Carnaroli or Arborio rice","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Do NOT rinse; starch is essential","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Mixed wild mushrooms (chanterelles, oyster, cremini)","amount":450,"unit":"g","notes":"Torn or sliced thick","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Rich mushroom or vegetable broth","amount":5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Kept simmering on adjacent burner","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Dry white wine (Pinot Grigio or Sauvignon Blanc)","amount":0.75,"unit":"cup","notes":"Room temp","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Shallots, finely minced","amount":2,"unit":"large","notes":"Brunoise","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Garlic cloves, minced","amount":4,"unit":"cloves","notes":"Divided","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh thyme leaves","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Finely chopped","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Parmigiano-Reggiano, freshly grated","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Finely microplaned","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Cold unsalted butter, cubed","amount":60,"unit":"g","notes":"Divided (for mantecatura)","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Extra virgin olive oil","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Divided","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh Italian flat-leaf parsley","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Minced for garnish","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Truffle oil (optional)","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Drizzled at the very end","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Sear Wild Mushrooms Hard","instruction":"Heat 1.5 tbsp olive oil and 1 tbsp butter in a cast iron skillet over high heat. Add wild mushrooms in a single layer. Sear without stirring for 3 mins until caramelized brown. Stir in 2 minced garlic cloves, thyme, salt, and pepper. Sauté 2 more mins. Remove from heat and set aside.","time":"6 mins","temp":"High heat (400°F / 205°C)","visualCue":"Deep bronze crisp edges with earthy woody perfume."},{"step":2,"title":"Tostatura (Toasting Rice)","instruction":"In a wide saucier, heat remaining oil and 1 tbsp butter over medium. Sweat minced shallots for 3 minutes until translucent. Pour in unwashed Carnaroli rice. Toast grains for 2-3 minutes, stirring continuously, until edges become translucent and kernels smell nutty.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Rice clicks against the pan sides with a dry, musical sound."},{"step":3,"title":"Sfumare (Deglazing with Wine)","instruction":"Pour in dry white wine. It will hiss dramatically. Stir continuously until wine is fully absorbed and the alcohol has evaporated.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"Pan dries up leaving aromatic, wine-soaked grains."},{"step":4,"title":"Ladle by Ladle Infusion","instruction":"Begin adding hot simmering broth, one ladle (about 3/4 cup) at a time. Stir frequently in sweeping strokes. Allow each addition to be almost entirely absorbed before adding the next ladle. Repeat for 16-18 minutes until rice is tender with a subtle al dente bite in center.","time":"18 mins","temp":"Gentle simmer","visualCue":"Starches release into a natural, luxurious creamy suspension."},{"step":5,"title":"Mantecatura (The Sacred Emulsion)","instruction":"Pull pan completely off the heat. Rest for 60 seconds. Vigorously beat in remaining cold cubed butter and microplaned Parmigiano-Reggiano. Fold in half the seared mushrooms. Spoon into warm shallow bowls, top with remaining crispy mushrooms, fresh parsley, and a whisper of truffle oil.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"Risotto flows in ripples like a gentle wave (''all''onda'') when you tilt the plate."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Keep the stock pot at a gentle simmer next to the risotto. Cold broth shocks the rice and halts starch release.","Mantecatura must be done OFF the heat so the cheese melts into an emulsion without separating into grease.","Don't rinse risotto rice! The powdery surface amylopectin starch is what creates the creamy sauce."',
  '[{"original":"Carnaroli rice","alternative":"Arborio or Vialone Nano rice","notes":"Carnaroli is the king of risotto, but Arborio is great."},{"original":"Parmigiano-Reggiano","alternative":"Pecorino Romano or nutritional yeast (vegan)","notes":"Pecorino adds extra sharp saltiness."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Washing the rice beforehand","remedy":"Washes away essential starch, resulting in watery rice instead of velvet risotto."},{"mistake":"Drowning rice with all the broth at once","remedy":"That makes boiled rice. Gradual agitation forces grains to rub together and create creaminess."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy"',
  'Stock must be piping hot; be careful when ladling into the hot pan.',
  'Best fresh. Leftovers can be shaped into balls, filled with mozzarella, and fried into Arancini!',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633964913295-ceb43826e7c9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~375g)","calories":450,"energyKj":1883,"protein":16,"carbohydrates":50,"sugar":6,"fiber":7,"totalFat":16,"saturatedFat":5,"sodium":540}'::jsonb
),
(
  'thai-green-curry-crisp-tofu',
  'thai-green-curry-crisp-tofu',
  'Aromatic Thai Green Coconut Curry with Golden Crisp Tofu',
  'Vibrant lemongrass & makrut lime broth with charred baby eggplants and sweet Thai basil',
  'A fragrant, herb-forward Southeast Asian curry. Crispy cubed organic tofu simmered in a luscious broth of cold-pressed coconut milk, bruised lemongrass, fresh green chilies, galangal, kaffir lime leaves, and bamboo shoots, finished with an abundance of sweet holy basil.',
  'Asian',
  'Thai',
  '15 mins',
  15,
  '15 mins',
  15,
  '30 mins',
  4,
  'Easy',
  4.89,
  198,
  410,
  '"Vegan","Gluten-Free","Spicy","Quick Dinner","Thai","Vegetarian","Asian","Pescatarian","Nut-Free","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Large wok or deep skillet","Tofu press or heavy cutting board with weights","Slotted spoon"',
  '[{"name":"Extra firm tofu, pressed and cut into 1-inch cubes","amount":400,"unit":"g","notes":"Pat completely dry","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Full-fat coconut milk (canned)","amount":2,"unit":"cans (400ml each)","notes":"Do not shake; scoop the thick top cream","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Authentic Thai green curry paste","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Mae Ploy or homemade","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Thai round eggplants or Japanese eggplant","amount":200,"unit":"g","notes":"Quartered","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Bamboo shoot slices (drained)","amount":0.75,"unit":"cup","notes":"Canned or fresh","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Makrut lime leaves (kaffir lime)","amount":5,"unit":"leaves","notes":"Torn to release fragrant citrus oils","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh Thai bird''s eye chilies","amount":2,"unit":"whole","notes":"Slit lengthwise (adjust to heat taste)","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Palm sugar or light brown sugar","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Balances herbal spice","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Tamari or vegetarian fish sauce","amount":2.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Savory salty base","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh Thai holy basil leaves","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Packed; added at the absolute end","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Cornstarch (for crisping tofu)","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Dusted on tofu cubes","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Neutral cooking oil","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For pan-crisping tofu","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Steamed Jasmine rice","amount":3,"unit":"cups","notes":"Warm for serving","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Pan-Crisp the Tofu","instruction":"Toss pressed dry tofu cubes in cornstarch with a pinch of salt. Heat 2 tbsp oil in wok over high heat. Fry tofu in a single layer for 6-8 mins, turning occasionally until all sides are golden and crunchy. Transfer to paper towel lined plate.","time":"8 mins","temp":"High heat (375°F / 190°C)","visualCue":"Tofu develops a crackly, golden shell that stays crisp in sauce."},{"step":2,"title":"Crack the Coconut Cream","instruction":"In the same wok, spoon in 1/2 cup of the thick coconut cream from the top of the can. Heat over medium-high until coconut oil begins to separate and shimmer with fine droplets.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"Cream bubbles vigorously and glistens with clear coconut fat droplets."},{"step":3,"title":"Fry the Curry Paste","instruction":"Add the green curry paste into the cracked cream. Sauté vigorously for 2 minutes until intensely aromatic and the paste integrates with the oil.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Intense lemongrass and green chili fragrance fills the kitchen."},{"step":4,"title":"Simmer Broth & Vegetables","instruction":"Pour in remaining coconut milk, 1/2 cup vegetable broth, palm sugar, and tamari. Add quartered eggplant, bamboo shoots, and torn lime leaves. Bring to a gentle boil, then simmer for 8 minutes until eggplant is tender-soft.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium-low simmer","visualCue":"Eggplants turn tender and turn jade green; sauce achieves silky body."},{"step":5,"title":"The Thai Basil Flourish","instruction":"Stir in the crispy tofu cubes. Turn off the flame completely. Toss in the vibrant Thai basil leaves and fold gently until wilted by residual heat. Ladle into wide bowls alongside fragrant jasmine rice.","time":"1 min","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"Thai basil wilts slightly, releasing sweet anise aromas throughout the emerald broth."}]'::jsonb,
  '"'Cracking' the coconut cream first is the true Thai technique — it extracts natural coconut oil so you fry the paste without adding heavy outside grease.","Always add Thai basil with the heat turned off; cooking it further destroys its fresh licorice aroma and turns leaves dark.","Tear makrut lime leaves instead of cutting them to rupture the essential oil glands."',
  '[{"original":"Extra firm tofu","alternative":"King oyster mushrooms or plant-based chicken strips","notes":"Or shrimp/chicken if non-vegetarian."},{"original":"Thai basil","alternative":"Sweet Italian basil + pinch of ground anise","notes":"Captures the peppery licorice profile."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Shaking the coconut milk can","remedy":"You want the dense cream separated on top to fry the aromatics properly."},{"mistake":"Boiling basil leaves","remedy":"Boiling turns basil bitter and dull brown."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Soy"',
  'Mind hot oil splatters when frying tofu; keep water away from the pan.',
  'Store refrigerated up to 4 days. Keep crispy tofu separate if you prefer maximum crunch when reheating.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1455619452474-d2be8b1e70cd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~347g)","calories":410,"energyKj":1715,"protein":14,"carbohydrates":45,"sugar":5,"fiber":6,"totalFat":14,"saturatedFat":4,"sodium":492}'::jsonb
),
(
  'smoky-shakshuka-whipped-feta',
  'smoky-shakshuka-whipped-feta',
  'Smoky Harissa Shakshuka with Jammy Eggs & Whipped Feta',
  'Spiced skillet tomatoes with poached runny yolks, crumbled feta & grilled sourdough',
  'A rustic Mediterranean and North African breakfast marvel. Rich vine tomatoes stewed with charred red bell peppers, smoked paprika, cumin, and fiery rose harissa, cradling farm eggs until whites are set and yolks remain golden and jammy.',
  'Breakfast',
  'Middle Eastern / North African',
  '10 mins',
  10,
  '15 mins',
  15,
  '25 mins',
  4,
  'Easy',
  4.96,
  310,
  320,
  '"Quick Meals","Vegetarian","One-Pan","Brunch Classic","Middle Eastern / North African","Breakfast","Eggetarian","Nut-Free","High-Protein","Low-Sugar"',
  '"12-inch seasoned cast iron skillet with lid","Wooden spoon","Ladle or small bowl for cracking eggs"',
  '[{"name":"Extra virgin olive oil","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Robust cold-pressed","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Red bell pepper, thinly sliced into ribbons","amount":1,"unit":"large","notes":"Sweet pepper","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Yellow onion, thinly sliced","amount":1,"unit":"medium","notes":"Sweet or Spanish onion","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Garlic cloves, thinly sliced","amount":4,"unit":"cloves","notes":"Thin coins","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Rose harissa paste","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Spicy, smoky floral paste","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Ground cumin","amount":1.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Toasted","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Smoked Spanish paprika (pimentón)","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Warm smokiness","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Canned crushed San Marzano tomatoes","amount":800,"unit":"g","notes":"Sweet high-grade tomatoes","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Large pasture-raised eggs","amount":4,"unit":"eggs","notes":"Fresh eggs with tall orange yolks","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Greek sheep''s milk feta","amount":80,"unit":"g","notes":"Crumbled roughly","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Fresh cilantro and parsley, roughly chopped","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Bright herbaceous finish","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Crusty sourdough bread","amount":4,"unit":"thick slices","notes":"Toasted with olive oil","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Char the Peppers & Onions","instruction":"Heat olive oil in cast iron skillet over medium-high. Add sliced bell pepper and onions with 1/2 tsp salt. Sauté for 6-8 minutes until edges begin to char and caramelize with deep sweet flavor.","time":"7 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"Peppers soften and show attractive charred spots along the ribbons."},{"step":2,"title":"Bloom the Spices & Harissa","instruction":"Add garlic, cumin, smoked paprika, and rose harissa paste to the skillet. Cook, stirring constantly for 90 seconds until the spices bloom into the hot oil.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"The oil turns a fiery rust red and releases an intense warm aroma."},{"step":3,"title":"Reduce the Tomato Stew","instruction":"Pour in crushed tomatoes and season with black pepper and a pinch of sugar. Simmer uncovered over medium-low heat for 8 minutes until sauce thickens and sauce holds a furrow when scraped with a spoon.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium-low simmer","visualCue":"Sauce becomes dense and jammy rather than watery."},{"step":4,"title":"Create Wells & Poach the Eggs","instruction":"Use the back of a spoon to make 4 distinct craters in the bubbling sauce. Crack each egg into a small cup, then slide one egg into each well. Season egg whites with a flake of salt. Cover with lid and cook on low for 4-5 minutes.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Low heat","visualCue":"Egg whites turn opaque milky white while yolks remain glossy, soft, and trembling."},{"step":5,"title":"Garnish & Sourdough Dipping","instruction":"Remove lid immediately. Scatter crumbled feta over the sauce, shower with chopped parsley, cilantro, and freshly cracked black pepper. Serve right in the skillet alongside charred olive oil sourdough toasts.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"Feta softens gently in the heat; breaking a yolk floods the spiced tomato with rich yellow cream."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Crack eggs into a ramekin first before sliding into the sauce — this ensures clean separation and avoids eggshell mishaps.","Check the eggs after 3.5 minutes; residual skillet heat continues cooking them even after taking off the flame.","Cast iron retains heat like no other pan, keeping the dish piping hot throughout the entire meal."',
  '[{"original":"Pasture eggs","alternative":"Silken tofu slabs or chickpeas (vegan)","notes":"Simmer chickpeas right in the sauce for high protein."},{"original":"Rose harissa","alternative":"Calabrian chili paste or chipotle in adobo","notes":"Provides smokiness and punchy heat."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Leaving sauce too watery before adding eggs","remedy":"Watery sauce makes poached whites separate and turn rubbery."},{"mistake":"Walking away from the covered skillet","remedy":"Eggs go from perfectly jammy to hard-boiled in 60 seconds."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Eggs","Dairy","Gluten (bread)"',
  'The cast iron skillet handle will be extremely hot; wrap with a cloth sleeve or silicone grip.',
  'Best enjoyed immediately. Leftover sauce can be saved for up to 3 days and re-poached with fresh eggs.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1590412200988-a436970781fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~284g)","calories":320,"energyKj":1339,"protein":26,"carbohydrates":19,"sugar":3,"fiber":3,"totalFat":12,"saturatedFat":4,"sodium":448}'::jsonb
),
(
  'paneer-tikka-masala-charred-peppers',
  'paneer-tikka-masala-charred-peppers',
  'Smoked Paneer Tikka Masala with Charred Bell Peppers',
  'Golden seared artisanal paneer in a rich spiced cashew-tomato curry',
  'A royal North Indian banquet staple. Fresh block paneer marinated in ajwain, yogurt, and aromatic spices, blistered on high heat alongside crunchy bell peppers and red onions, then folded into a velvety spiced tomato gravy.',
  'Indian',
  'North Indian',
  '20 mins',
  20,
  '25 mins',
  25,
  '45 mins',
  4,
  'Medium',
  4.94,
  260,
  520,
  '"Vegetarian","High-Protein","Comfort Food","Gluten-Free","North Indian","Indian"',
  '"Cast iron skillet or griddle","Deep kadai or Dutch oven","High speed blender","Tongs"',
  '[{"name":"Fresh firm paneer, cut into 1.5-inch cubes","amount":450,"unit":"g","notes":"Soaked in warm salted water for 10 mins","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Hung curd or thick Greek yogurt","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Strained","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Red and green bell peppers, cut into squares","amount":2,"unit":"peppers","notes":"For tikka skewers/sear","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Red onion, cut into petals","amount":1,"unit":"large","notes":"Layers separated","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Mustard oil","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Smoked to smoking point for pungency","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Kashmiri red chili powder","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Divided for color and spice","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Ajwain (carom seeds)","amount":0.5,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Crushed in palm","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Kasuri methi (fenugreek)","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Lightly toasted","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Canned tomato puree","amount":2,"unit":"cups","notes":"Smooth puree","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Cashew paste","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Cashews blended with warm water","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Garam masala","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Aromatic finishing spice","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Fresh cream","amount":0.25,"unit":"cup","notes":"For finishing swirl","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Ghee or butter","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Cooking fat","category":"Dairy"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Marinate Paneer & Veggies","instruction":"Heat mustard oil until smoking, cool slightly, then stir in 1 tbsp Kashmiri chili for vibrant red oil. Whisk with Greek yogurt, ginger-garlic paste, ajwain, garam masala, and salt. Coat paneer cubes, bell peppers, and onion petals. Marinate for 30 minutes.","time":"30 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Paneer and vegetables are clad in a rich, spicy scarlet coat."},{"step":2,"title":"Char the Tikka","instruction":"Heat a cast iron skillet over high heat with 1 tbsp ghee. Sear paneer, peppers, and onions in batches for 2-3 minutes per side until blistered with smoky spots. Do not overcook paneer.","time":"8 mins","temp":"High heat (425°F / 220°C)","visualCue":"Paneer edges are golden and crispy, while center remains pillow-soft."},{"step":3,"title":"Build the Masala Gravy","instruction":"In a Dutch oven, melt 1 tbsp ghee. Add cumin seeds, minced onion, and sauté until golden brown (8 mins). Stir in ginger-garlic paste, remaining chili powder, coriander powder, and tomato puree. Cook until oil separates from the masala.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Red oil beads gather on the perimeter of the bubbling masala."},{"step":4,"title":"Enrich with Cashews & Simmer","instruction":"Stir in cashew paste and 1/2 cup warm water. Simmer on low for 5 minutes until glossy. Gently fold in the charred paneer, blistered peppers, and onions.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Low simmer","visualCue":"Gravy clings lovingly to every cube of charred paneer."},{"step":5,"title":"Finish with Kasuri Methi & Cream","instruction":"Swirl in fresh heavy cream and crushed kasuri methi. Turn off heat. Cover for 2 minutes to let aromas marry. Serve with steaming jeera rice or butter naan.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"Sunset-hued gravy with swirls of ivory cream and herbal green leaves."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Soaking paneer in warm salted water for 10 minutes beforehand keeps the interior extraordinarily soft throughout frying.","Heating mustard oil until it smokes removes raw pungency while imparting that signature tandoor depth.","Avoid boiling after paneer is added; excessive heat turns paneer rubbery."',
  '[{"original":"Paneer","alternative":"Extra firm pressed tofu or halloumi","notes":"Tofu makes this recipe 100% vegan."},{"original":"Cashew paste","alternative":"Sunflower seed paste or almond flour","notes":"Great nut-free alternative."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Over-searing the paneer","remedy":"Paneer only needs 2 mins per side; cooking longer dehydrates the cheese."},{"mistake":"Rushing the onion browning","remedy":"Deep golden onions give the masala its foundational sweet savory backbone."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy","Tree Nuts (Cashews)"',
  'Smoking mustard oil generates strong vapors; turn on your kitchen exhaust fan.',
  'Refrigerate up to 4 days. When reheating, add 2 tbsp warm milk to restore sauce consistency.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1565557623262-b51c2513a641?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~424g)","calories":520,"energyKj":2176,"protein":18,"carbohydrates":57,"sugar":7,"fiber":8,"totalFat":18,"saturatedFat":5,"sodium":624}'::jsonb
),
