  '"Quick Meals","Seafood","Italian","Weeknight Hero","Italian-American / Coastal Italian","Pescatarian","Nut-Free","High-Protein","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Large pasta pot","12-inch stainless steel or cast iron skillet","Pasta tongs","Citrus squeezer"',
  '[{"name":"Linguine pasta","amount":350,"unit":"g","notes":"Bronze-die extruded pasta for texture","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Jumbo wild shrimp (peeled, deveined, tails on)","amount":500,"unit":"g","notes":"Patted dry with paper towels","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Garlic cloves, thinly shaved into chips","amount":6,"unit":"cloves","notes":"Shaved with razor-sharp knife","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Crushed red pepper flakes (or Calabrian chili)","amount":0.75,"unit":"tsp","notes":"For gentle back-heat","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Dry crisp white wine (Pinot Grigio)","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Sauce base","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh lemon juice + zest","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Zest before juicing","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Unsalted butter (cold cubes)","amount":60,"unit":"g","notes":"Swirled in at end for sheen","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Extra virgin olive oil","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"High quality oil","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh Italian flat-leaf parsley, finely chopped","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Bright herbaceous bite","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Flaky sea salt & freshly ground black pepper","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"To taste","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Cook Linguine Al Dente","instruction":"Bring a large pot of salted water (like the sea) to a roaring boil. Drop linguine and cook 1 minute less than package directions. Reserve 1 cup starchy pasta cooking water before draining.","time":"9 mins","temp":"Rolling boil","visualCue":"Pasta retains a white pinpoint core of firmness when bitten."},{"step":2,"title":"Quick-Sear the Shrimp","instruction":"Heat 1 tbsp olive oil and 1 tbsp butter in large skillet over high heat. Add shrimp in a single layer. Season with salt and black pepper. Sear for 90 seconds per side until pink and curled into a loose ''C'' shape. Transfer immediately to a warm plate.","time":"3 mins","temp":"High heat (375°F / 190°C)","visualCue":"Shrimp turn pearlescent pink; do not overcook until curled tight like an ''O''."},{"step":3,"title":"Golden Garlic & Wine Deglaze","instruction":"Lower heat to medium. Add remaining olive oil, shaved garlic chips, and chili flakes. Sauté for 60 seconds until garlic is pale straw gold (do not brown). Pour in white wine and lemon juice. Scrape up brown bits and boil down by half.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Liquid reduces into a glistening reduction; garlic fragrance is mellow and sweet."},{"step":4,"title":"Emulsify Sauce with Cold Butter","instruction":"Turn heat to low. Whisk in remaining cold cubed butter piece by piece alongside 1/4 cup reserved starchy pasta water. Whisk briskly until an opaque, creamy emulsion forms.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Low heat","visualCue":"Butter and wine combine into a glossy, velvety pan glaze."},{"step":5,"title":"Toss with Pasta & Herbs","instruction":"Add drained linguine and cooked shrimp back to the skillet. Toss vigorously with tongs over medium heat for 60 seconds so pasta drinks in the sauce. Stir in lemon zest and chopped parsley. Serve immediately in warm bowls.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Every noodle is cloaked in shimmering garlic butter and flecked with emerald parsley."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Shrimp shape rule: 'C' means Cooked, 'O' means Overcooked! Take them out the second they form a 'C'.","Starchy pasta water is the secret culinary glue that binds melted butter and wine into a velvety sauce instead of a greasy pool.","Slice garlic into razor-thin chips rather than mincing — minced garlic burns too easily in high heat."',
  '[{"original":"Shrimp","alternative":"Sea scallops, chunks of halibut, or sliced chicken breast","notes":"Sear scallops 2 mins per side."},{"original":"White wine","alternative":"Seafood or chicken stock + extra lemon juice","notes":"Maintains acidity without alcohol."}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Burning the garlic chips","remedy":"Burnt garlic turns acrid and bitter; if it browns too fast, dump pan and restart."},{"mistake":"Dumping pasta water down the drain","remedy":"Always scoop out a mug of starchy water before pouring pasta into the colander."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Crustacean Shellfish","Dairy","Gluten"',
  'Thoroughly pat shrimp dry before searing to prevent oil spitting.',
  'Best eaten immediately. Leftovers can be kept refrigerated for up to 2 days; warm gently over low heat in a skillet.',
