  '"Heavy bottom skillet / wok","Mortar and pestle or spice grinder"',
  '[{"name":"Chicken thighs, cut into bite-sized pieces","amount":700,"unit":"g","notes":"Bone-in or boneless","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Black peppercorns","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Whole black tellicherry","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Fennel seeds (saunf) & cumin","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Toasted","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Small shallots (sambar onions), sliced","amount":15,"unit":"whole","notes":"Essential for sweetness","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh curry leaves","amount":3,"unit":"sprigs","notes":"Aromatic","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Ginger-garlic paste","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Fresh","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Gingelly (sesame) oil or coconut oil","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Authentic Chettinad medium","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Roast Fresh Chettinad Spice","instruction":"Dry toast black peppercorns, fennel seeds, cumin, and dry red chilies for 2 minutes until fragrant. Grind into a coarse aromatic powder.","time":"4 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Deep pepper fragrance fills the kitchen."},{"step":2,"title":"Caramelize Shallots & Curry Leaves","instruction":"Heat gingelly oil. Sauté shallots and generous curry leaves until translucent and golden. Add ginger-garlic paste and cook 2 minutes.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Shallots turn glossy brown and sweet."},{"step":3,"title":"Sear Chicken in Spice Paste","instruction":"Add chicken pieces, turmeric, and half the ground pepper masala. Sear on high heat for 5 minutes until chicken is sealed.","time":"5 mins","temp":"High heat","visualCue":"Chicken is coated in dark brown spice base."},{"step":4,"title":"Slow Simmer to Reduction","instruction":"Add 1 cup water, cover and simmer 15 minutes. Uncover, add remaining black pepper spice, and cook down until sauce clings thickly to the chicken.","time":"15 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Glistening dark pepper gravy coating each piece."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Using small shallots (sambar onions) provides natural caramelized sweetness to balance the heavy black pepper heat.","Adding half the pepper masala at the beginning and the rest at the end delivers both deep infused warmth and fresh aroma."',
  '[{"original":"Chicken","alternative":"Paneer cubes or baby mushrooms","notes":"Sensational vegetarian pepper fry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Using pre-ground black pepper powder","remedy":"Pre-ground pepper tastes flat and bitter; only use freshly toasted whole peppercorns."}]'::jsonb,
