  '"Clay pot (Meen Chatti) or shallow Dutch oven"',
  '[{"name":"Firm white fish steaks (Kingfish, Sea Bass, or Salmon)","amount":600,"unit":"g","notes":"Cleaned & patted dry","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Kudampuli (Malabar tamarind)","amount":3,"unit":"pieces","notes":"Soaked in warm water 15 mins","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Thick coconut milk (first press)","amount":0.75,"unit":"cup","notes":"Creamy finish","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Thin coconut milk (second press)","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Simmering base","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Shallots, thinly sliced","amount":10,"unit":"whole","notes":"Aromatics","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Ginger juliennes & green chilies","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Slit chilies","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Kashmiri chili powder & turmeric","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Vibrant yellow-orange base","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Cold-pressed coconut oil","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Authentic coastal fat","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Sauté Aromatics in Coconut Oil","instruction":"Heat coconut oil in clay pot. Add mustard seeds, fenugreek seeds, curry leaves, ginger, and shallots. Cook until fragrant and translucent.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Aroma of toasted coconut and popping mustard."},{"step":2,"title":"Simmer Spices & Thin Coconut Milk","instruction":"Add chili powder, turmeric, coriander, soaked Kudampuli with water, and thin coconut milk. Simmer for 8 minutes.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Curry turns glowing fiery orange and bubbles gently."},{"step":3,"title":"Poach Fish Steaks","instruction":"Carefully slide fish steaks into the bubbling curry. Swirl the pot gently by its handles—never stir with a spoon to avoid breaking the fish. Simmer 8 minutes.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium-low heat","visualCue":"Fish turns opaque, tender, and absorbs the tart sauce."},{"step":4,"title":"Finish with Thick Coconut Milk","instruction":"Lower heat and pour in thick coconut milk. Gently swirl and remove from heat immediately before it boils.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"Velvety, rich orange gravy with fragrant coconut aroma."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Swirling the earthenware pot instead of stirring with a ladle prevents delicate fish flakes from breaking.","Kudampuli provides a smoky tang distinct from regular tamarind."',
  '[{"original":"Kudampuli","alternative":"Kokum rinds or raw mango slices","notes":"Provides clean sour note"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Boiling thick coconut milk vigorously","remedy":"High heat splits coconut milk; add at the very end on low heat."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Fish"',
  'Clay pots remain extremely hot; use dry pot holders when swirling.',
  'Authentic fish curry is legendary for tasting best on day 2 and day 3.',
