  '"High-Protein","Festive","Signature","Dinner","Traditional","Hyderabadi","Indian","Vegetarian","Nut-Free"',
  '"Heavy bottom biryani handi with tight lid","Large pasta pot for parboiling rice","Tawa for indirect heat"',
  '[{"name":"Extra-long grain aged basmati rice","amount":500,"unit":"g","notes":"Soaked 45 mins","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Bone-in chicken or goat pieces","amount":800,"unit":"g","notes":"Raw marinated","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Crispy fried golden onions (birista)","amount":2,"unit":"cups","notes":"Divided in marinade & layering","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Full-fat plain yogurt (curd)","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Whisked smooth","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Ginger-garlic paste","amount":2.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Freshly pounded","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Shahi jeera, green cardamom & mace","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Royal spices","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Saffron strands steeped in warm milk","amount":0.25,"unit":"cup","notes":"For golden aroma","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Pure desi ghee","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Poured over rice","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Fresh mint & cilantro leaves","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Finely chopped","category":"Produce"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Marinate the Meat","instruction":"Rub meat with yogurt, half the fried onions, ginger-garlic paste, chili powder, shahi jeera, mace, mint, cilantro, and salt. Marinate at least 3 hours.","time":"15 mins + chill","temp":"Refrigerated","visualCue":"Meat is deeply coated in rich spiced marinade."},{"step":2,"title":"Parboil Basmati to 70%","instruction":"Boil 8 cups salted water with green cardamom, bay leaves, and cloves. Add soaked rice. Cook for exactly 5 minutes until rice is 70% cooked (grain bends without snapping). Drain immediately.","time":"7 mins","temp":"Rolling boil","visualCue":"Rice grains elongate and feel firm at core."},{"step":3,"title":"Layer Meat & Rice","instruction":"Place raw marinated meat across the bottom of the handi. Layer warm parboiled rice on top. Scatter remaining fried onions, chopped herbs, saffron milk, and melted ghee.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"Pristine white rice crowned with herbs, gold saffron, and caramelized onions."},{"step":4,"title":"Dum Steam Seal","instruction":"Seal lid edges with flour dough. Cook on high heat for 10 minutes, then place handi over a hot cast-iron tawa on low heat for 35 minutes to steam gently.","time":"45 mins","temp":"Indirect low heat","visualCue":"Lid seal is puffed and dry; steam escapes with heady saffron aroma when cracked open."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Parboiling the rice to precisely 70% is essential; the meat releases steam that finishes cooking the grains to separate, fluffy perfection.","Using a tawa underneath the handi prevents the meat from burning at the bottom during dum."',
  '[{"original":"Chicken / Goat","alternative":"Paneer, mushrooms, and seasonal vegetables","notes":"For Hyderabadi Dum Vegetable Biryani"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Opening the lid during dum","remedy":"Keep completely sealed so steam pressure remains trapped."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy"',
  'Steam is intensely hot when breaking the dough seal.',
  'Refrigerate up to 4 days; rice remains moist and aromatic.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1563379091339-03b21ab4a4f8?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
  false,
