  'The pinnacle of Bengali monsoon gastronomy. Delicate, sweet Hilsa fish (or sea bass) is gently simmered in a sharp, pungent emulsion of freshly ground yellow and brown mustard seeds, turmeric, and slit green chilies in pure mustard oil.',
