  '"High-Protein","Gluten-Free","Dinner","Signature","Festive","Bengali","Indian","Nut-Free","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Heavy cast iron Dutch oven or kadai","Pressure cooker (optional)"',
  '[{"name":"Bone-in goat meat or lamb, cut in pieces","amount":800,"unit":"g","notes":"Trimmed","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Red onions, thinly sliced","amount":4,"unit":"large","notes":"Caramelized deeply","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Mustard oil","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Pungent base","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Plain yogurt","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Tenderizer","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Sugar","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"For onion caramelization","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Bengali garam masala & bay leaf","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Cardamom, cinnamon, clove","category":"Spices"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Marinate Mutton","instruction":"Toss mutton with yogurt, ginger-garlic paste, turmeric, mustard oil, and salt. Marinate 2 hours.","time":"10 mins + chill","temp":"Refrigerated","visualCue":"Mutton is evenly coated and tenderizing."},{"step":2,"title":"Caramelize Onions to Dark Amber","instruction":"Heat mustard oil in pot. Add pinch sugar to caramelize, followed by sliced onions. Fry slowly for 20 mins until rich dark chocolate brown.","time":"20 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Deep amber onions that provide the signature dark hue."},{"step":3,"title":"The ''Koshano'' Slow Roast","instruction":"Add marinated meat and spices. Fry and stir continuously (''koshano'') for 25 minutes without water until oil separates and meat darkens.","time":"25 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Dark mahogany glossy gravy clinging to tender meat."},{"step":4,"title":"Slow Braise to Tenderness","instruction":"Add 1.5 cups warm water, cover and simmer on low for 30 minutes (or pressure cook 4 whistles) until meat is fork-tender.","time":"30 mins","temp":"Low simmer","visualCue":"Meat pulls apart easily from bone in rich dark sauce."}]'::jsonb,
  '"The technique of 'koshano' (slow-roasting spices and meat in its own rendered fat) is what gives this dish its deep caramelized flavor.","Sugar in the hot oil melts into caramel that gives the rich dark color."',
  '[{"original":"Mutton","alternative":"Beef chuck or bone-in chicken thighs","notes":"Adjust cooking time accordingly"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Rushing onion browning","remedy":"Pale onions result in pale, watery curry; take time to achieve dark chocolate brown."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy"',
  'Slow-roasting can create hot oil spatters; stir with long-handled wooden spoon.',
  'Refrigerate up to 4 days; flavor only gets better.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1545247181-516773cae754?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
  false,
