  '"Vegetarian","Vegan","Gluten-Free","Breakfast","Snack","Street Food","Quick Meals","Gujarati","Indian","Jain-Friendly","Dairy-Free","Nut-Free"',
  '"Steamer or large pot with rack","8-inch cake pan","Toothpick"',
  '[{"name":"Besan (fine gram/chickpea flour)","amount":200,"unit":"g","notes":"Sifted","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Semolina (sooji)","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For texture","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fruit salt (Eno) or baking soda","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Aerating agent","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Lemon juice & sugar","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Sweet-sour balance","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Mustard seeds & white sesame seeds","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Tempering","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Green chilies, slit & fresh cilantro","amount":3,"unit":"whole","notes":"Garnish","category":"Produce"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Whisk Aerated Batter","instruction":"Whisk besan, semolina, lemon juice, sugar, turmeric, pinch salt, and 1 cup water until smooth and lump-free. Rest 10 mins.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Smooth golden batter that flows like pancake batter."},{"step":2,"title":"Aerate & Steam Immediately","instruction":"Grease cake pan. Stir fruit salt briskly into batter for 10 seconds. Pour foaming batter into pan and steam on high for 15 minutes.","time":"15 mins","temp":"High steam","visualCue":"Batter bubbles up into a fluffy sponge; toothpick comes out clean."},{"step":3,"title":"Prepare Sizzling Sugar-Tamarind Temper","instruction":"Heat 1 tbsp oil in pan. Sauté mustard seeds, sesame, curry leaves, and green chilies. Add 0.5 cup water and 1 tbsp sugar. Bring to a boil.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Aromatic sweet-savory tempering water."},{"step":4,"title":"Soak & Cut Diamond Cubes","instruction":"Cut warm steamed dhokla into cubes. Spoon warm tempering liquid evenly over sponge so it absorbs completely. Garnish with fresh coconut and cilantro.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Warm","visualCue":"Moist, incredibly juicy and springy golden cubes."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Always steam immediately after adding fruit salt; delaying will let the trapped carbon dioxide escape.","Pouring warm tempering water over warm dhokla guarantees a melt-in-mouth, non-choking sponge."',
  '[{"original":"Fruit salt (Eno)","alternative":"0.5 tsp baking soda + 1 tsp lemon juice","notes":"Standard pantry substitute"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Using too much turmeric","remedy":"Excess turmeric reacts with baking soda turning red; use just a tiny pinch."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Sesame"',
  'Beware of hot steam when opening steamer lid.',
  'Keeps moist and delicious in fridge for up to 3 days.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1505253716362-afaea1d3d1af?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
  false,
  '{"servingSize":"1 portion (~214g)","calories":220,"energyKj":920,"protein":6,"carbohydrates":29,"sugar":22,"fiber":2,"totalFat":10,"saturatedFat":6,"sodium":77}'::jsonb
),
(
  'dal-baati-churma-royal',
  'dal-baati-churma-royal',
  'Royal Rajasthani Dal Baati Churma',
  'Hard-baked whole wheat dough balls dipped in pure desi ghee, served with five-lentil dal and sweet crumbled churma',
  'The pride of Rajasthan''s warrior heritage. Hearty whole-wheat baatis are baked until cracked, steeped in pure molten ghee, and paired with spicy Panchmel dal (five lentils) and sweet cardamom-infused churma crumble.',
  'Indian',
