  '"Wide flat skillet or tawa","Potato masher"',
  '[{"name":"Boiled potatoes, cauliflower & peas","amount":500,"unit":"g","notes":"Cooked soft","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Finely chopped tomatoes","amount":400,"unit":"g","notes":"Juicy ripe Roma","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Green bell pepper, finely minced","amount":1,"unit":"large","notes":"Crunchy note","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Salted butter","amount":100,"unit":"g","notes":"Generous butter for bhaji & pav","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Pav bhaji masala powder","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Street-style blend","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Kashmiri chili powder","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For street-red color","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Soft pav bread buns","amount":8,"unit":"rolls","notes":"Slit horizontally","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Sauté Vegetables & Butter","instruction":"Melt 40g butter on a wide skillet. Add finely chopped onions, minced bell pepper, and ginger-garlic paste. Cook 5 mins until soft.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Aromatic sizzle with melting butter."},{"step":2,"title":"Add Tomatoes & Spices","instruction":"Add chopped tomatoes, pav bhaji masala, Kashmiri chili, and salt. Cook until tomatoes completely break down into mush.","time":"6 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Glossy red paste bubbling on pan."},{"step":3,"title":"Mash Directly on Tawa","instruction":"Add boiled potatoes, cauliflower, and peas with 1 cup water. Use a potato masher vigorously on the pan until smooth and uniformly blended. Simmer 10 mins with extra butter.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Low-medium heat","visualCue":"Rich, luscious, thick orange-red bhaji."},{"step":4,"title":"Toast Pav in Spiced Butter","instruction":"Melt 2 tbsp butter on skillet with pinch of pav bhaji masala and cilantro. Press slit pav onto the spiced butter and toast until golden and warm.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Pillowy buns soaked with fragrant golden butter."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Mashing directly on the hot flat tawa creates emulsified starch that gives the bhaji its famous glossy, smooth texture.","Toasting the bread in spiced butter rather than plain butter elevates it to true Mumbai street cart quality."',
  '[{"original":"Pav buns","alternative":"Dinner rolls or brioche buns","notes":"Soft rolls work wonderfully"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Skimping on butter","remedy":"Authentic pav bhaji relies on butter for its signature flavor and sheen."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten","Dairy"',
  'Press potato masher firmly without letting hot vegetable steam burn fingers.',
  'Bhaji freezes great for up to 2 months; keeps in fridge for 4 days.',
