  '"High-Protein","Gluten-Free","Dairy-Free","Dinner","Signature","Traditional","Kashmiri","Indian","Vegetarian","Nut-Free"',
  '"Heavy bottom pot or Dutch oven","Mortar and pestle"',
  '[{"name":"Bone-in lamb or goat meat, cut into cubes","amount":800,"unit":"g","notes":"Trimmed","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Kashmiri red chili powder","amount":2.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Whisked with warm water","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Fennel seed powder (saunf)","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Signature Kashmiri sweet aroma","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Dry ginger powder (sonth)","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Warm piquant note","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Asafoetida (hing)","amount":0.25,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Dissolved in water","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Mustard oil","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Smoked & cooled","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Green cardamom, black cardamom & cloves","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Whole aromatics","category":"Spices"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Sear Lamb in Smoked Mustard Oil","instruction":"Heat mustard oil in pot until smoking, then lower heat. Add hing, cloves, and cardamoms. Sear lamb pieces on high heat for 10 mins until golden brown.","time":"12 mins","temp":"High heat","visualCue":"Lamb develops browned edges."},{"step":2,"title":"Whisk Chili & Spice Paste","instruction":"Mix Kashmiri chili powder with 0.5 cup warm water. Pour into the seared lamb and fry 5 mins until the oil absorbs the brilliant red color.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Liquid turns deep glowing scarlet."},{"step":3,"title":"Add Fennel & Ginger Infusion","instruction":"Stir in fennel powder, dry ginger powder, and salt with 2 cups warm water. Bring to a boil.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Aromatic sweet fennel fragrance blooms."},{"step":4,"title":"Slow Simmer to Tenderness","instruction":"Cover tightly and simmer on low for 45 minutes until lamb is completely tender and oil separates at surface.","time":"45 mins","temp":"Low simmer","visualCue":"Glossy red rogan oil floating on silky lamb gravy."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Traditional Kashmiri Rogan Josh never uses onions, garlic, or tomatoes; its body and complex flavor come entirely from fennel powder, dry ginger, and Kashmiri chilies.","Whisking the chili powder in water before adding prevents it from burning in the hot oil."',
  '[{"original":"Lamb","alternative":"Bone-in chicken thighs or baby mushrooms","notes":"Adjust cooking time accordingly"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Adding onions or garlic","remedy":"Traditional Pandit style Rogan Josh relies strictly on hing and spices."}]'::jsonb,
  '{}',
  'Let mustard oil smoke gently to remove raw pungency, then cool slightly before adding meat.',
  'Refrigerate up to 4 days; flavor deepens overnight.',
