  '"High-Protein","Comfort Food","Festive","Dinner","Signature","Hyderabadi","Indian","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Heavy bottom pot or pressure cooker","Heavy wooden masher / pestle (ghotna)"',
  '[{"name":"Boneless lamb or mutton","amount":600,"unit":"g","notes":"Cut into chunks","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Cracked wheat (daliya) & pearl barley","amount":150,"unit":"g","notes":"Soaked 2 hours","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Lentils mix (chana, toor, moong, masoor)","amount":100,"unit":"g","notes":"Soaked","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Desi ghee","amount":100,"unit":"g","notes":"Divided in cooking & topping","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Fried crispy golden onions (birista)","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"For layering & garnish","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Shahi garam masala, green chilies & mint","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Aromatics","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Fresh lime wedges & roasted cashew nuts","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Essential topping","category":"Produce"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Cook Meat with Aromatics","instruction":"Cook mutton with ginger-garlic paste, half the ghee, fried onions, garam masala, and 3 cups water until meat shreds apart effortlessly.","time":"30 mins","temp":"High pressure","visualCue":"Meat is tender enough to shred with a spoon."},{"step":2,"title":"Boil Wheat & Lentils","instruction":"In another pot, boil cracked wheat, barley, and lentils with 4 cups water until soft and porridge-like. Mash coarsely.","time":"25 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Lentils and wheat break down into thick paste."},{"step":3,"title":"The ''Ghotna'' Beating Technique","instruction":"Combine shredded meat and cooked lentils in a heavy pot. Using a wooden masher, vigorously beat and pound the mixture against the pot sides for 20 minutes until the meat fibers shred and blend with the wheat into a stretchy, cohesive texture.","time":"20 mins","temp":"Low heat","visualCue":"Haleem forms long, stretchy savory ribbons."},{"step":4,"title":"Garnish & Ghee Finish","instruction":"Swirl in remaining molten ghee. Serve hot crowned with crispy fried onions, fresh mint leaves, toasted cashews, and a squeeze of lime.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Hot","visualCue":"Glistening ghee pooling over thick, rich brown porridge."}]'::jsonb,
  '"The traditional beating (ghotna) is essential; it breaks down the meat fibers into long threads that give Haleem its signature stretchy, velvety texture.","Always serve with plenty of fresh lime; the acid cuts through the richness of the ghee and meat."',
  '[{"original":"Mutton","alternative":"Chicken thighs","notes":"Chicken Haleem cooks in half the time"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Pureeing in a blender","remedy":"A blender cuts meat fibers into a paste; use a masher to preserve stretchy meat threads."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten","Dairy","Nuts"',
  'Pot gets very heavy and hot during pounding; secure on stove.',
  'Refrigerate up to 5 days; freezes wonderfully for up to 2 months.',
