  '"Deep kadai for frying","Slotted spoon"',
  '[{"name":"Boiled potatoes, peeled & mashed","amount":450,"unit":"g","notes":"Lumpy potato mash","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Besan (gram/chickpea flour)","amount":150,"unit":"g","notes":"For batter","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Mustard seeds, curry leaves & green chilies","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For tempering potato","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Dry garlic-peanut chutney (lasun chutney)","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Signature Mumbai dry spice","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Soft pav buns","amount":8,"unit":"buns","notes":"Slit horizontally","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Salted fried green chilies","amount":8,"unit":"whole","notes":"Traditional accompaniment","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Oil for deep frying","amount":3,"unit":"cups","notes":"Clean frying oil","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Prepare Spiced Potato Balls","instruction":"Temper mustard seeds, curry leaves, hing, minced garlic, ginger, and turmeric in 1 tbsp oil. Stir into mashed potatoes with cilantro and salt. Roll into 8 golf-ball sized rounds.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Vibrant yellow, fragrant potato spheres."},{"step":2,"title":"Whisk Crispy Besan Batter","instruction":"Whisk chickpea flour, pinch turmeric, salt, baking soda, and water into a smooth batter that coats the back of a spoon.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Smooth golden batter."},{"step":3,"title":"Dip & Deep Fry Vadas","instruction":"Dip each potato ball into batter, ensuring complete coat. Slide gently into 360°F hot oil. Fry for 4-5 minutes until crisp and golden. Drain on paper towels.","time":"5 mins","temp":"360°F (180°C)","visualCue":"Golden amber, crispy round fritters with tender potato inside."},{"step":4,"title":"Assemble the Mumbai Burger","instruction":"Spread green chutney on bottom bun, dry red garlic chutney on top. Place hot vada in center, press bun down gently, and serve with fried salted green chili.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Hot","visualCue":"Iconic street food slider ready to bite."}]'::jsonb,
  '"The dry garlic-peanut chutney is what separates genuine Mumbai vada pav from ordinary potato sliders; make it by blending fried garlic, roasted peanuts, and chili powder.","Fry extra batter drips in the hot oil to make crunchy 'chura' to scatter inside the bun."',
  '[{"original":"Pav buns","alternative":"Brioche slider buns or dinner rolls","notes":"Soft rolls work great"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Making the batter too thin","remedy":"If batter is watery, it will slide off the potato ball in the hot oil."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten","Nuts"',
  'Slit green chilies before frying or they will pop in hot oil.',
  'Vadas must be eaten fresh and hot.',
