  'Crispy spiral-layered coiled flatbread served with caramelized shallot & fennel meat roast',
  'The supreme culinary icon of Northern Kerala. Maida dough is oiled, beaten, stretched paper-thin, pleated into spirals, and griddled with pure ghee into shatteringly flaky golden layers, paired with a dark caramelized onion, curry leaf, and coconut sliver meat roast.',
