  '[{"name":"All-purpose flour (maida)","amount":400,"unit":"g","notes":"Rested & oiled","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Desi ghee or coconut oil","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For spiral pleating","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Bone-in tender beef or mutton","amount":600,"unit":"g","notes":"For roast curry","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Shallots (small onions), sliced","amount":2,"unit":"cups","notes":"Caramelized dark","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Coconut slices (thenga kothu)","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Fried crunchy bits","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fennel seeds, black pepper & curry leaves","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Key roast spices","category":"Spices"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Knead & Pleat Parotta Spirals","instruction":"Knead flour, water, pinch sugar, and oil into pliable dough. Rest 1 hour. Stretch paper-thin on oiled counter, pleat like an accordion, roll into tight snail spirals, and rest 15 mins.","time":"20 mins + rest","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Translucent layered dough spirals."},{"step":2,"title":"Slow Roast Meat with Coconut Slices","instruction":"Pressure cook meat with turmeric, pepper, and coriander. Sauté shallots, ginger, garlic, and coconut slices in coconut oil until dark amber. Add meat and roast on medium until gravy clings dry.","time":"25 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Dark mahogany, spicy caramelized meat roast with crispy coconut chips."},{"step":3,"title":"Griddle & Clasp Parottas","instruction":"Gently roll spirals into rounds. Griddle on hot tawa with ghee on both sides until golden brown with crisp spots.","time":"6 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"Golden brown rings and blisters."},{"step":4,"title":"The Two-Hand Clasp","instruction":"Stack 3 hot parottas. Firmly clap hands against sides to separate the flaky layers.","time":"1 min","temp":"Hot","visualCue":"Parottas puff into hundreds of wispy, featherlight flaky shreds."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Clapping the hot cooked parottas between your palms immediately off the tawa releases trapped steam and fluffs open the dozens of crisp spiral layers.","Coconut slices (thenga kothu) fried in coconut oil add the signature Malabar crunch."',
  '[{"original":"Meat roast","alternative":"Mushroom or paneer roast","notes":"Vegetarian pairing"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Rolling spirals with heavy pressure","remedy":"Roll very gently with minimal pressure so layers don''t crush together."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten","Dairy"',
  'Parottas are hot when clapping; tap briskly.',
