  'Golden Crispy Medu Vada with Sambar',
  'Crisp-shelled, doughnut-shaped white lentil fritters with fluffy airy center & fresh coconut chutney',
  'The classic South Indian breakfast icon. Dehulled black gram lentils (urad dal) are ground into an aerated, cloud-like batter with crushed black peppercorns, ginger, and curry leaves, shaped into rings and fried until shatteringly crisp outside and pillowy soft inside.',
