  '"Wet grinder or food processor","Deep frying kadai","Slotted spoon"',
  '[{"name":"Whole skinless urad dal (soaked 4 hours)","amount":250,"unit":"g","notes":"Drained cold","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Whole black peppercorns & cumin seeds","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Coarsely crushed","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Fresh curry leaves, chopped & green chilies","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Aromatics","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Finely chopped ginger & fresh coconut bits","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Crunch","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Oil for deep frying","amount":3,"unit":"cups","notes":"Clean frying oil","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Aerate Batter with Minimal Water","instruction":"Grind drained urad dal with just 2-3 tbsp ice-cold water, aerating continuously until light, fluffy, and doubles in volume. Test: a drop of batter should float on water.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Chilled","visualCue":"Cloud-like, airy white batter that floats like foam."},{"step":2,"title":"Fold Seasonings","instruction":"Stir in crushed peppercorns, cumin, ginger, green chilies, curry leaves, coconut bits, and salt. Beat with hand for 1 minute.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Herb-flecked fluffy batter."},{"step":3,"title":"Shape with Water-Wet Palm","instruction":"Wet hands with water. Take a portion of batter on fingers, make a hole in center with thumb like a doughnut, and slide gently into 360°F hot oil.","time":"3 mins","temp":"360°F (180°C)","visualCue":"Doughnut ring puffs instantly into oil."},{"step":4,"title":"Fry until Golden Amber","instruction":"Fry for 4-5 minutes, turning over until evenly golden brown and crisp. Drain and serve hot with coconut chutney and hot sambar.","time":"5 mins","temp":"360°F (180°C)","visualCue":"Shatteringly crisp golden ring with steaming, airy cotton interior."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Use ice-cold water while grinding dal to prevent the grinder motor heat from warming the batter, which makes vadas absorb excess oil.","The water float test is foolproof: if a small drop of batter floats on a cup of water, your vadas will be cloud-light."',
