  'The Sunday morning royal breakfast of Bengal. Tissue-thin, snow-white puffed flatbreads (luchi) made from refined flour are fried in ghee, paired with spicy, tangy baby potatoes slow-cooked in cumin, ginger, and pungent asafoetida (hing).',
