  '[{"step":1,"title":"Knead Supple Luchi Dough","instruction":"Rub ghee into flour until crumbly. Add warm water and knead into a supple, non-sticky dough. Rest 20 mins under damp cloth.","time":"10 mins + rest","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Pliable, smooth snow-white dough."},{"step":2,"title":"Slow Simmer Alur Dom","instruction":"Fry boiled baby potatoes until golden. In mustard oil, sizzle bay leaf, hing, and ginger paste. Add pureed tomatoes, turmeric, and cumin. Simmer potatoes in gravy for 12 mins.","time":"15 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Thick, dark crimson gravy clinging to potatoes."},{"step":3,"title":"Roll & Fry Snow-White Luchis","instruction":"Roll dough balls into thin 4-inch rounds with oil. Slide into 375°F hot oil. Press gently with slotted ladle until it puffs completely into a white sphere. Flip for 15 seconds.","time":"5 mins","temp":"375°F (190°C)","visualCue":"Puffed, pristine white balloon bread."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Fry luchis for only 30-40 seconds total; unlike pooris, authentic Bengali luchis must remain snow-white without browning.","Bhaja moshla (dry roasted cumin and dry red chili powder) sprinkled at the end gives the signature Kolkata flavor."',
