  '[{"step":1,"title":"Velvet the Chicken","instruction":"Toss diced chicken with 1 tbsp soy sauce, 1 tbsp Shaoxing wine, and 1 tbsp cornstarch. Rest 10 minutes to lock in moisture.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Chicken is coated in a thin protective starch glaze."},{"step":2,"title":"Whisk Kung Pao Sauce","instruction":"Mix black vinegar, light soy sauce, dark soy sauce, sugar, chicken stock, and 1 tsp cornstarch until sugar dissolves.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Glossy dark brown sauce."},{"step":3,"title":"Bloom Spices in Wok","instruction":"Heat oil in smoking hot wok. Fry dried chilies and Sichuan peppercorns for 30 seconds until darkened and fragrant.","time":"1 min","temp":"High heat","visualCue":"Chilies turn dark ruby and peppercorns sizzle."},{"step":4,"title":"Wok-Sear Chicken & Peanuts","instruction":"Add chicken and stir-fry briskly on high heat for 3 mins. Add garlic, ginger, and scallions. Pour in sauce and toss until bubbling and thick. Stir in peanuts and serve immediately.","time":"4 mins","temp":"High heat","visualCue":"Glossy mahogany sauce clings to crisp chicken and crunchy peanuts."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Velveting the chicken with cornstarch ensures it stays tender and juicy even under intense wok heat.","Chinkiang black vinegar provides the signature complex malty acidity of true Sichuan cuisine."',
  '[{"original":"Peanuts","alternative":"Roasted cashews","notes":"Sweet, crunchy substitute"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Burning dried chilies","remedy":"Keep wok moving constantly; chilies turn bitter if blackened completely."}]'::jsonb,
