  '"High-Protein","Street Food","Comfort Food","Dinner","Signature","Korean","Asian","Gluten-Free","Dairy-Free"',
  '"Deep fryer or heavy Dutch oven","Thermometer","Wire cooling rack"',
  '[{"name":"Chicken wings & drumettes","amount":1,"unit":"kg","notes":"Patted bone-dry","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Potato starch or cornstarch","amount":0.75,"unit":"cup","notes":"Key to glass-like crunch","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Korean gochujang (fermented red pepper paste)","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Sweet-spicy glaze","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Raw honey or rice syrup (mulyeot)","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Sticky sheen","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Minced garlic & fresh ginger","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Aromatics","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Toasted white sesame seeds & chopped peanuts","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Garnish","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Frying oil","amount":4,"unit":"cups","notes":"High smoke point oil","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Season & Coat in Starch","instruction":"Toss dry chicken wings with pinch salt, black pepper, and minced ginger. Dredge thoroughly in potato starch until completely coated.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Even white powdery coating without damp spots."},{"step":2,"title":"First Fry (Render & Cook)","instruction":"Fry wings in 325°F (165°C) oil for 10 minutes until pale golden and cooked through. Drain on wire rack for 10 minutes.","time":"10 mins","temp":"325°F (165°C)","visualCue":"Pale golden with firm crust."},{"step":3,"title":"Second Flash Fry (Glass Crunch)","instruction":"Increase oil temperature to 375°F (190°C). Fry wings a second time for 3-4 minutes until deeply golden and shatteringly crunchy.","time":"4 mins","temp":"375°F (190°C)","visualCue":"Deep amber color; wings sound like glass when tapped with tongs."},{"step":4,"title":"Bubble Glaze & Toss","instruction":"Simmer gochujang, honey, soy sauce, garlic, and vinegar in wok for 2 mins until bubbling. Toss crispy chicken briskly until lacquered. Sprinkle with sesame seeds.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Glossy, sticky scarlet glaze hugging crunch."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Potato starch (not all-purpose flour) is the secret behind the paper-thin, glass-like crunch of Korean fried chicken.","The double-fry technique draws out trapped steam in the second fry so the chicken stays crisp even after being glazed."',
  '[{"original":"Chicken wings","alternative":"Cauliflower florets or firm tofu cubes","notes":"Incredible vegan KFC"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Only frying once","remedy":"Single frying produces wings that turn soggy minutes after saucing."}]'::jsonb,
