  '"Steamer with cheesecloth / bamboo steamer basket","Small saucepan"',
  '[{"name":"Thai sweet glutinous rice (sticky rice)","amount":300,"unit":"g","notes":"Soaked in water 4 hours","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Full-fat coconut milk (canned)","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Divided in rice soak & sauce","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Palm sugar or granulated sugar","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Sweetness balance","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Sea salt","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Critical sweet-salty contrast","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Ripe yellow honey mangoes (Ataulfo or Nam Dok Mai)","amount":2,"unit":"large","notes":"Chilled & sliced","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Toasted yellow split mung beans (or sesame seeds)","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Crunchy topping","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Steam Glutinous Sticky Rice","instruction":"Drain soaked sticky rice. Wrap in cheesecloth and steam over boiling water for 20 minutes until translucent and tender.","time":"20 mins","temp":"High steam","visualCue":"Glistening, translucent tender rice grains."},{"step":2,"title":"Warm Coconut Infusion","instruction":"In a saucepan, heat 1 cup coconut milk with sugar and 0.5 tsp salt until dissolved. Do not boil.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Low heat","visualCue":"Warm, sweet fragrant coconut cream."},{"step":3,"title":"Steep Rice in Coconut Cream","instruction":"Transfer hot steamed rice to a bowl. Pour warm coconut cream over. Stir gently, cover tightly with plate, and rest 20 mins for rice to absorb liquid.","time":"20 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Rice swells into glossy, rich coconut pearl grains."},{"step":4,"title":"Assemble with Sweet Mango","instruction":"Simmer remaining 0.5 cup coconut milk with pinch salt and rice flour until thick. Plate warm sticky rice, arrange fan of chilled mango slices alongside, drizzle with sauce, and scatter toasted mung beans.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Warm rice / Chilled fruit","visualCue":"Golden mango fan against pearlescent coconut rice."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Do not skip the salt in the coconut cream; the salty-sweet contrast is what elevates Thai mango sticky rice above ordinary desserts.","Steaming the rice in a cheesecloth ensures the grains cook evenly without becoming water-logged."',
  '[{"original":"Mung beans","alternative":"Toasted white sesame seeds","notes":"Nutty crunch"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Boiling sticky rice in water like Jasmine rice","remedy":"Sticky rice MUST be steamed; boiling makes it gummy mush."}]'::jsonb,
  '{}',
  'Handle hot steamer basket with tongs.',
  'Eat fresh on the day made; refrigerated sticky rice turns hard.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1551024601-bec78aea704b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
