  '"Soup pot","Ladle"',
  '[{"name":"Jumbo tiger prawns or river prawns (heads on)","amount":450,"unit":"g","notes":"Heads provide rich prawn oil","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Fresh lemongrass stalks, bruised & sliced diagonally","amount":3,"unit":"stalks","notes":"Aromatics","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh galangal root, thinly sliced","amount":1,"unit":"chunk (5cm)","notes":"Zesty aromatic","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Kaffir lime leaves, torn to release oil","amount":6,"unit":"leaves","notes":"Citrus perfume","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Thai bird''s eye chilies, crushed lightly","amount":6,"unit":"whole","notes":"Fiery heat","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Oyster or straw mushrooms","amount":200,"unit":"g","notes":"Halved","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Thai chili paste (Nam Prik Pao) & fish sauce","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Color & umami","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh lime juice","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Added OFF heat for bright acid","category":"Produce"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Boil Aromatic Infusion","instruction":"Bring 4 cups water or chicken stock to a boil. Add bruised lemongrass, galangal slices, torn kaffir lime leaves, and crushed chilies. Simmer 5 mins to extract oils.","time":"6 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"Intensely fragrant citrus-herbal aroma fills room."},{"step":2,"title":"Add Mushrooms & Chili Jam","instruction":"Stir in Nam Prik Pao chili paste, fish sauce, and straw mushrooms. Cook 3 minutes until broth turns shimmering sunset orange.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Glowing crimson-orange broth with herbal floating islands."},{"step":3,"title":"Poach Prawns Gently","instruction":"Add cleaned prawns with heads intact. Simmer for 3 minutes until prawns turn pink and curl into tender crescents. Remove from heat immediately.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Medium-low heat","visualCue":"Prawns turn opaque pink with rich orange prawn butter in broth."},{"step":4,"title":"Off-Heat Lime Finish","instruction":"Take pot off heat and stir in fresh lime juice and fresh cilantro leaves. Taste and adjust sweet-sour-spicy balance before serving.","time":"1 min","temp":"Off heat","visualCue":"Piping hot, aromatic, electric citrus broth."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Always add fresh lime juice after turning off the heat; boiling lime juice causes it to become bitter and destroys its vibrant floral top notes.","Using head-on prawns releases natural prawn butter (tomalley) that gives the soup its authentic orange sheen."',
  '[{"original":"Prawns","alternative":"Sliced chicken breast (Tom Yum Gai) or firm tofu","notes":"Poultry or vegetarian"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Eating the lemongrass and galangal stalks","remedy":"These are meant for flavoring the broth only; push to the side of the bowl."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Shellfish","Fish"',
  'Crush chilies gently with back of knife; do not rub eyes.',
  'Best enjoyed fresh; reheated broth loses crisp lime freshness.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548943487-a2e4e43b4853?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
