  '[{"step":1,"title":"Crisp the Baguette","instruction":"Toast baguette in 375°F (190°C) oven for 3-4 minutes until the crust is shatteringly crisp to the touch.","time":"4 mins","temp":"375°F (190°C)","visualCue":"Crust flakes and crackles like delicate glass."},{"step":2,"title":"Slit & Spread Pâté & Mayo","instruction":"Slice baguette lengthwise, leaving one hinge. Spread generous layer of mayonnaise on one side and smooth pork liver pâté on the other.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Warm","visualCue":"Velvety coating of rich spreads."},{"step":3,"title":"Layer Meats & Pickles","instruction":"Layer sliced Chả Lụa pork and roasted meats. Top with drained pickled carrots and daikon, crisp cucumber spears, and spicy jalapeño rounds.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Colorful contrast of pink meat, orange carrot, and green cucumber."},{"step":4,"title":"Herb Crown & Maggi Drops","instruction":"Tuck in generous sprigs of cilantro, dash 3-4 drops of Maggi seasoning, close sandwich, and enjoy immediately.","time":"1 min","temp":"Fresh","visualCue":"Stunning street sandwich with loud crackling bite."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Vietnamese baguettes contain rice flour in the dough, which creates an ultra-thin, crackling crust with an airy crumb that doesn't feel dense.","Do not skip the pâté; its rich umami is the flavor bridge connecting the savory meats and sweet-tangy pickles."',
