  '"Pizza stone or baking steel","Pizza peel","Oven on max broil"',
  '[{"name":"Tipo 00 Italian flour","amount":500,"unit":"g","notes":"High protein wheat flour","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Instant dry yeast","amount":2,"unit":"g","notes":"Slow cold fermentation","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Canned San Marzano D.O.P. whole tomatoes","amount":400,"unit":"g","notes":"Crushed by hand with sea salt","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh buffalo mozzarella (Mozzarella di Bufala)","amount":250,"unit":"g","notes":"Torn & drained well","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Fresh basil leaves","amount":15,"unit":"leaves","notes":"Picked fresh","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Extra virgin olive oil (cold-pressed)","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Top quality Italian oil","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Knead & Cold Ferment Dough","instruction":"Mix flour, water (65% hydration), yeast, and salt. Knead 10 mins until silky smooth. Ball into 4 portions and cold ferment in fridge for 24-48 hours.","time":"15 mins + chill","temp":"Refrigerated","visualCue":"Air pockets develop beneath elastic translucent skin."},{"step":2,"title":"Preheat Baking Steel","instruction":"Place pizza steel on highest rack. Preheat oven to 550°F (290°C) for 60 minutes until steel is blazing hot.","time":"60 mins","temp":"550°F (290°C)","visualCue":"Steel radiates intense, shimmering dry heat."},{"step":3,"title":"Hand-Stretch & Dress","instruction":"Press dough ball from center outward with fingertips, pushing air into the rim (cornicione). Top with hand-crushed tomatoes, torn mozzarella, basil, and olive oil.","time":"4 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Raised puffy rim with light, un-weighed center."},{"step":4,"title":"Blistering Hot Bake","instruction":"Slide onto preheated steel under full broil. Bake for 4-5 minutes until the crust puffs dramatically with dark leopard spots.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Broil Max","visualCue":"Charred leopard spots, bubbling cheese, and fragrant basil."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Crush San Marzano tomatoes by hand rather than in a blender; blending incorporates air and shears seeds, making sauce watery and acidic.","Tear mozzarella onto a paper towel 30 minutes before baking to eliminate liquid that makes pizza soggy."',
  '[{"original":"Buffalo mozzarella","alternative":"Low-moisture whole milk mozzarella","notes":"Great melt without excess water"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Using a rolling pin on pizza dough","remedy":"Rolling pins crush all delicate gas bubbles; always stretch with your fingertips."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten","Dairy"',
  'Baking steel reaches near 600°F; handle pizza peel with extreme care.',
  'Best fresh; re-crisp leftovers in a dry cast iron skillet with a lid.',
