  '"High-Protein","Quick Meals","Under 30 mins","Dinner","Signature","Italian","Vegetarian","Nut-Free"',
  '"Wide stainless steel or aluminum pan","Microplane grater","Tongs"',
  '[{"name":"Bronze-cut Italian Spaghetti","amount":400,"unit":"g","notes":"Rough textured surface","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Guanciale (cured pork jowl), cut into lardons","amount":180,"unit":"g","notes":"Traditional Roman cured meat","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Farm fresh egg yolks","amount":4,"unit":"large","notes":"Plus 1 whole egg","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Pecorino Romano cheese, finely grated","amount":100,"unit":"g","notes":"Aged, sharp sheep milk cheese","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Whole black peppercorns","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Toasted & coarsely cracked","category":"Spices"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Render Guanciale Lardons","instruction":"Place guanciale in a cold pan over medium-low heat. Slowly render the clear fat until pieces turn crisp and golden brown on the outside but tender inside. Turn off heat.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium-low heat","visualCue":"Crisp amber nuggets floating in clear golden rendered fat."},{"step":2,"title":"Whisk Egg-Pecorino Paste","instruction":"Whisk egg yolks, whole egg, grated Pecorino Romano, and cracked black pepper in a bowl into a thick, uniform paste.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Thick, rich golden cheese paste."},{"step":3,"title":"Boil Spaghetti Al Dente","instruction":"Boil spaghetti in moderately salted water until 2 minutes shy of package al dente. Reserve 1 cup of cloudy starchy pasta water.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Rolling boil","visualCue":"Spaghetti has firm, white core when bitten."},{"step":4,"title":"Emulsify Off the Flame","instruction":"Transfer pasta directly into the warm pan with rendered guanciale. Splash with 4 tbsp pasta water. Take pan completely off heat. Pour in egg-cheese paste and toss vigorously until a silky, creamy sauce wraps every strand.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Off heat (residual heat only)","visualCue":"Lustrous, glossy creamy coat with zero scrambled egg clumps."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Never add the egg-cheese mixture over active flame; residual heat from the pasta water and pan is sufficient to cook the eggs into silk without scrambling.","Guanciale has a higher fat content and sweeter herb cure than bacon or pancetta."',
  '[{"original":"Guanciale","alternative":"Pancetta or thick-cut smoked bacon","notes":"Common butcher alternative"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Adding heavy cream or peas","remedy":"Real Roman carbonara gets 100% of its creaminess from cheese, yolk, and pasta water starch."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten","Dairy","Eggs"',
  'Toss vigorously off flame to temper eggs gently.',
  'Carbonara must be eaten immediately; reheating scrambles the delicate egg emulsion.',
