  '"15-inch Spanish carbon steel paella pan","Wide burner or gas grill"',
  '[{"name":"Spanish Bomba or Calasparra short-grain rice","amount":400,"unit":"g","notes":"Absorbs 3x its volume in liquid","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Chicken thighs, cut into bite-sized pieces","amount":600,"unit":"g","notes":"Bone-in for rich stock","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Spanish saffron threads, steeped in warm water","amount":0.5,"unit":"g","notes":"Golden aroma and color","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Flat green beans (Romano beans) & butter beans (Garrofó)","amount":250,"unit":"g","notes":"Classic vegetables","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Sweet smoked Spanish paprika (Pimentón de la Vera)","amount":1,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Smoky sweet","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Grated ripe tomatoes","amount":2,"unit":"large","notes":"Pulp only, skins discarded","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh rosemary sprig","amount":1,"unit":"sprig","notes":"Placed on top last 5 mins","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Extra virgin olive oil","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Spanish oil","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Sear Chicken in Paella Pan","instruction":"Heat olive oil in wide paella pan over medium heat. Brown chicken pieces with salt for 10 minutes until deeply golden on all sides. Push meat to edges of pan.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Crisp, golden-brown chicken pieces."},{"step":2,"title":"Sauté Beans & Sofrito","instruction":"In the center of pan, sauté green beans and butter beans for 4 minutes. Add grated tomatoes and smoked paprika. Stir 2 minutes until liquid evaporates into a jammy sofrito.","time":"6 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Dark red sofrito bubbling in pan center."},{"step":3,"title":"Add Saffron Stock & Distribute Rice","instruction":"Pour in 6 cups rich warm broth and steeped saffron. Bring to a rolling boil. Rain the Bomba rice across the pan in a cross pattern, then spread evenly. Do not stir again!","time":"10 mins","temp":"High boil","visualCue":"Golden-yellow saffron broth bubbling around nestled rice."},{"step":4,"title":"Simmer & Achieve Socarrat","instruction":"Lower heat to medium-low and simmer 10 minutes until liquid is absorbed. Place rosemary sprig on top. Increase heat to medium-high for 2 minutes—listen for a distinct crackling sound. Rest 5 minutes covered with a kitchen towel before serving.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Low heat then high burst","visualCue":"Audible crackle and irresistible toasted caramelized rice aroma from pan bottom."}]'::jsonb,
  '"The absolute golden rule of authentic paella: once you distribute the rice in the boiling stock, NEVER stir it again; stirring releases starches that make it creamy like risotto instead of separate and crisp.","Listen closely at the end: when the sound changes from bubbling to a gentle rhythmic crackle, your socarrat crust is forming."',
  '[{"original":"Chicken","alternative":"Prawns, mussels, and calamari","notes":"Paella de Marisco (Seafood Paella)"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Stirring the rice during simmering","remedy":"Never stir; let the rice absorb the liquid undisturbed."}]'::jsonb,
  '{}',
  'Wide paella pan handles get extremely hot; use dual heat pads.',
  'Best enjoyed immediately straight out of the pan.',
