  '"High-Protein","Street Food","Dinner","Signature","Quick Meals","Greek","European","Nut-Free","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Grill pan or outdoor barbecue","Wooden skewers (soaked)"',
  '[{"name":"Boneless skinless chicken thighs, cut into 1-inch cubes","amount":750,"unit":"g","notes":"Juicy cut for grilling","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Greek extra virgin olive oil & fresh lemon juice","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Classic marinade","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Wild dried Greek oregano & minced garlic","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Herbal backbone","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Authentic Greek strained yogurt (tzatziki)","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Thick & creamy","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"English cucumber, grated & squeezed dry","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Tzatziki base","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Fresh dill, minced garlic & red wine vinegar","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Tzatziki seasoning","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Greek pita flatbreads","amount":4,"unit":"pitas","notes":"Oiled & grilled","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Marinate Chicken Skewers","instruction":"Toss chicken cubes with olive oil, lemon juice, oregano, garlic, salt, and black pepper. Thread onto soaked skewers and marinate for 1 hour.","time":"10 mins + chill","temp":"Refrigerated","visualCue":"Chicken glazes in herb-speckled olive oil marinade."},{"step":2,"title":"Whip Cool Garlic Tzatziki","instruction":"Grate cucumber and squeeze out every drop of water in clean towel. Mix into thick Greek yogurt with minced garlic, fresh dill, vinegar, and olive oil.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Chilled","visualCue":"Thick, creamy pale green dip that holds its shape."},{"step":3,"title":"Char-Grill Souvlaki","instruction":"Grill chicken skewers over screaming-hot grill or cast-iron grill pan for 10-12 minutes, turning frequently until nicely charred and cooked through.","time":"12 mins","temp":"High heat","visualCue":"Smoky grill marks and sizzling herb-charred edges."},{"step":4,"title":"Grill Pita & Plate","instruction":"Brush pitas with olive oil and grill 1 minute until puffed and warm. Slide hot chicken off skewers onto pita, add thick tzatziki, sliced tomatoes, and red onion.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Hot & Cold contrast","visualCue":"Juicy charred chicken with cool refreshing garlic dip."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Squeeze all moisture out of the grated cucumber in a tea towel before adding to yogurt; excess water makes tzatziki runny.","Chicken thighs stay much juicier and more forgiving over high grill heat than chicken breasts."',
  '[{"original":"Chicken","alternative":"Lamb cubes or halloumi cheese","notes":"Classic Greek variations"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Using thin, watery regular yogurt for tzatziki","remedy":"Only use authentic strained Greek yogurt."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Dairy","Gluten"',
  'Soak wooden skewers in water for 30 mins before grilling to prevent burning.',
  'Tzatziki keeps 5 days in fridge; chicken keeps 3 days.',
