  'Texas Hill Country Smoked Beef Brisket',
  'Slow-smoked whole packer beef brisket with black pepper bark, mahogany smoke ring & rendered juicy fat',
  'The Holy Grail of Central Texas barbecue. Whole packer beef brisket is rubbed simply with equal parts coarse kosher salt and 16-mesh black pepper, slow-smoked for 12 hours over post oak wood until the bark is jet-black, the smoke ring is deep pink, and the meat bends like gelatin under its own weight.',
