  '"Oven or smoker with wood chips","Heavy butcher paper","Meat thermometer"',
  '[{"name":"Whole beef brisket flat or point (trimmed)","amount":2,"unit":"kg","notes":"1/4-inch fat cap maintained","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Coarse 16-mesh black pepper","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Texas Dalmatian rub","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Coarse kosher salt","amount":3,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"1:1 ratio with pepper","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Garlic powder","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Optional accent","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Apple cider vinegar spray","amount":0.5,"unit":"cup","notes":"Moisture spritz","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Trim & Dalmatian Rub","instruction":"Trim hard deckle fat, leaving 1/4-inch uniform fat cap on flat. Coat thoroughly with equal parts coarse black pepper and kosher salt. Rest 30 mins.","time":"20 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Even gravel-like coating of black pepper and white salt."},{"step":2,"title":"Low & Slow Smoke","instruction":"Cook at 250°F (120°C) with wood smoke for 4-5 hours, spritzing with apple cider vinegar hourly until an intense jet-black bark develops (165°F internal).","time":"180 mins","temp":"250°F (120°C)","visualCue":"Crisp, jet-black glistening pepper bark."},{"step":3,"title":"The Texas Crutch Wrap","instruction":"Wrap tightly in pink butcher paper with rendered beef tallow. Return to heat until internal temperature reaches 203°F and probe slides in like warm butter.","time":"60 mins","temp":"250°F (120°C)","visualCue":"Meat yields completely with zero resistance when probed."},{"step":4,"title":"Long Rest & Slice","instruction":"Rest wrapped brisket in a dry cooler for at least 1-2 hours. Slice against the grain into pencil-thick slices.","time":"60 mins","temp":"Resting","visualCue":"Vivid pink smoke ring, glistening juices dripping from slice that bends over your finger."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Coarse 16-mesh black pepper is essential; fine table pepper turns into a paste that blocks smoke penetration.","Resting wrapped brisket in an insulated cooler for 2 hours allows all rendered collagen to redistribute into pure tenderness."',
