  '"Heavy bottom Dutch oven or cast iron pot","Foil for tight steam seal"',
  '[{"name":"Long grain parboiled rice","amount":500,"unit":"g","notes":"Rinsed until water runs clear","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Ripe Roma tomatoes & red bell peppers (tatashe)","amount":600,"unit":"g","notes":"Blended base","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Scotch bonnet peppers (ata rodo)","amount":2,"unit":"whole","notes":"Fierce fruity heat","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Tomato paste","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Deep umami color","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Dried thyme, Nigerian curry powder & bay leaves","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Signature seasoning","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Rich chicken or vegetable stock","amount":2.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Broth base","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Ripe yellow plantains (dodo)","amount":2,"unit":"large","notes":"Sliced diagonally & fried","category":"Produce"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Blend & Reduce Pepper Puree","instruction":"Blend tomatoes, red bell peppers, onions, and Scotch bonnets until smooth. Boil in a saucepan for 15 minutes to reduce liquid by half.","time":"15 mins","temp":"Medium-high heat","visualCue":"Thick, concentrated orange-red paste."},{"step":2,"title":"Fry Tomato Paste Base","instruction":"Heat vegetable oil in Dutch oven. Sauté sliced onions and tomato paste for 6 minutes until dark brick red. Stir in reduced pepper puree, curry powder, thyme, and bay leaves until oil floats.","time":"12 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Glossy red oil separating at the edges."},{"step":3,"title":"Steam Rice with Tight Foil Seal","instruction":"Stir washed parboiled rice and hot stock into pot. Cover pot mouth tightly with heavy aluminum foil, then clamp lid down. Simmer on lowest heat for 30 minutes.","time":"30 mins","temp":"Lowest simmer","visualCue":"Trapped steam fluffs rice grains without burning."},{"step":4,"title":"Party Smoky Char & Serve with Dodo","instruction":"Increase heat slightly for the final 3 minutes to develop famous ''party smokiness'' at the bottom. Fluff with fork and serve with golden fried sweet plantains.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Glistening orange rice grains that separate cleanly with sweet golden dodo."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Sealing the pot with aluminum foil under the lid traps the steam so the rice cooks in the concentrated pepper essence rather than needing excess water.","The gentle scorch at the bottom of the pot creates that beloved 'party smoke' aroma that defines wedding Jollof."',
  '[{"original":"Scotch bonnet","alternative":"Habanero pepper","notes":"Identical heat and fruity profile"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Adding too much stock","remedy":"Excess liquid makes soggy, mushy rice; Jollof cooks primarily from trapped steam."}]'::jsonb,
