  '"High-Protein","Gluten-Free","Dinner","Signature","Quick Meals","Turkish","Vegetarian","Middle Eastern","Dairy-Free","Nut-Free"',
  '"Wide flat metal skewers","Charcoal grill or grill pan"',
  '[{"name":"Ground lamb shoulder with 20% fat","amount":650,"unit":"g","notes":"Cold, finely minced","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Sweet red bell pepper (or Kapia pepper)","amount":1,"unit":"large","notes":"Minced very fine & squeezed dry","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Turkish Urfa or Aleppo chili flakes (Pul Biber)","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Smoky sweet heat","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Red onion, thinly sliced with sumac & parsley","amount":1.5,"unit":"cups","notes":"Traditional salad","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Warm Turkish lavash or pita flatbreads","amount":4,"unit":"pieces","notes":"Charred","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Knead Meat until Sticky","instruction":"Knead minced lamb, squeezed red pepper, chili flakes, and salt for 5 minutes until meat proteins develop a sticky, tacky texture.","time":"6 mins","temp":"Chilled","visualCue":"Tacky meat mixture that easily adheres to hands."},{"step":2,"title":"Mold onto Flat Skewers","instruction":"With water-wet hands, mold meat around wide flat skewers in rippled accordion shapes. Chill 30 mins to firm up.","time":"6 mins + chill","temp":"Refrigerated","visualCue":"Even, rippled meat kebabs firmly secured on flat skewers."},{"step":3,"title":"High-Heat Charcoal Grill","instruction":"Grill over hot charcoal (or grill pan) for 8-10 minutes, flipping frequently so fat drips onto bread without falling off skewers.","time":"10 mins","temp":"High heat","visualCue":"Sizzling charred fat, smoky aroma, and juicy pink center."},{"step":4,"title":"Slide into Lavash & Serve","instruction":"Using warm lavash as a mitt, slide meat off skewer. Top with sumac-dressed onions, grilled tomatoes, and serve immediately.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Hot","visualCue":"Juicy, smoky spiced lamb resting on herb-dusted flatbread."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Kneading the ground meat until sticky develops myosin protein, which prevents the meat from falling off the skewers during grilling.","Use wide, flat swords rather than thin round skewers."',
  '[{"original":"Lamb","alternative":"80/20 ground beef chuck","notes":"Widely made beef Adana"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Using lean meat","remedy":"Lean meat turns dry and falls off skewers; 20% fat is essential."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Gluten (if served with bread)"',
  'Metal skewers get very hot; use insulated gloves.',
  'Eat fresh off the grill.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1529193591184-b1d58069ecdd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
