  'ethiopian-doro-wat-injera',
  'ethiopian-doro-wat-injera',
  'Ethiopian Royal Doro Wat with Injera',
  'Slow-braised chicken & hard-boiled eggs in fiery berbere spice, niter kibbeh spiced butter & spongy sourdough injera',
  'The crown celebration dish of Ethiopian cuisine. Tender chicken drumsticks and thighs are slow-braised for hours with melted spiced clarified butter (niter kibbeh), aromatic berbere spice blend, caramelized onions, and whole hard-boiled eggs, served over spongy sourdough teff flatbread (injera).',
