  '"Dutch oven or clay pot","Large communal serving platter"',
  '[{"name":"Bone-in chicken drumsticks & thighs","amount":800,"unit":"g","notes":"Skinless, pierced with fork","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Red onions, pureed or finely minced","amount":4,"unit":"large","notes":"Slowly caramelized dry","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Authentic Ethiopian Berbere spice blend","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Complex sweet chili spice","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Niter Kibbeh (Ethiopian spiced clarified butter)","amount":4,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Infused with korarima & garlic","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Hard-boiled eggs, pierced with knife","amount":4,"unit":"whole","notes":"Simmered in gravy","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Injera flatbreads (fermented teff bread)","amount":4,"unit":"breads","notes":"Spongy base","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Dry Sweat Pureed Onions","instruction":"Cook minced onions in a dry Dutch oven without oil for 25 minutes, stirring continuously until moisture evaporates and onions turn sweet amber paste.","time":"25 mins","temp":"Low-medium heat","visualCue":"Dark amber, jammy reduced onion paste."},{"step":2,"title":"Bloom Berbere & Niter Kibbeh","instruction":"Add Niter Kibbeh spiced butter and Berbere spice. Sauté for 10 minutes until deep crimson oil separates.","time":"10 mins","temp":"Medium-low heat","visualCue":"Intensely fragrant, dark scarlet bubbling sauce."},{"step":3,"title":"Braise Chicken & Eggs","instruction":"Add chicken pieces, garlic, ginger, and 1 cup water. Simmer covered for 30 minutes. Add pierced hard-boiled eggs and simmer 10 more minutes until sauce thickens.","time":"40 mins","temp":"Low simmer","visualCue":"Chicken is fall-apart tender; eggs stained crimson."},{"step":4,"title":"Communal Injera Presentation","instruction":"Line large platter with injera bread. Ladle hot Doro Wat in center, arrange eggs around, and eat communally with torn pieces of injera.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Hot","visualCue":"Regal crimson stew resting on spongy grey-brown teff bread."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Cooking the onions dry without any oil first is the essential Ethiopian technique that concentrates the onion sugars.","Injera bread acts as both the platter and the utensil; tear pieces with your right hand to scoop the chicken and sauce."',
  '[{"original":"Niter kibbeh","alternative":"Ghee infused with cardamom, fenugreek, and garlic","notes":"Homemade alternative"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Rushing onion cooking","remedy":"The 25-minute onion reduction creates the velvety body of the stew."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Eggs","Dairy"',
  'Berbere can be fiery; adjust quantity to your heat tolerance.',
  'Refrigerates for up to 5 days; flavor deepens overnight.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1512058564366-18510be2db19?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
  false,
