  '"Dutch oven","Baking sheet for crisping under broiler"',
  '[{"name":"Pork shoulder (Boston butt), cut into 2-inch chunks","amount":1.2,"unit":"kg","notes":"Well-marbled","category":"Proteins"},{"name":"Fresh orange juice & orange halves","amount":1,"unit":"orange","notes":"Natural citrus tenderizer","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Mexican oregano, cumin & bay leaves","amount":1.5,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Traditional seasoning","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Sweetened condensed milk or evaporated milk","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Authentic Michoacán browning secret","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Corn tortillas, limes & salsa verde","amount":1,"unit":"serving","notes":"For taco assembly","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Slow Confit Braise","instruction":"Place pork chunks in Dutch oven with orange juice, squeezed orange halves, evaporated milk, oregano, garlic, bay leaves, and 1 cup water. Simmer covered on low for 80 minutes until pork is tender.","time":"80 mins","temp":"Low simmer","visualCue":"Pork chunks yield easily when pierced with fork."},{"step":2,"title":"Shred into Large Chunks","instruction":"Remove pork from braising liquid. Coarsely pull into large bite-sized chunks using two forks.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Room temp","visualCue":"Juicy, tender shredded pork shreds."},{"step":3,"title":"Broil for Crackling Charred Edges","instruction":"Spread shredded pork on baking sheet, drizzle with 3 tbsp braising fat, and broil on high for 5 minutes until tips turn dark golden and crispy.","time":"5 mins","temp":"Broil High","visualCue":"Glistening mahogany crispy shreds with tender succulent centers."},{"step":4,"title":"Serve in Hot Corn Tortillas","instruction":"Mound hot crispy carnitas into warm corn tortillas. Top with diced white onion, fresh cilantro, lime juice, and salsa verde.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Hot","visualCue":"Street food perfection with crisp juicy meat."}]'::jsonb,
  '"A splash of evaporated or condensed milk in the braise is the traditional Michoacán street vendor secret that caramelizes the pork edges to amber perfection under the broiler.","Do not shred the pork too finely; leave large, succulent chunks."',
  '[{"original":"Pork shoulder","alternative":"Chicken thighs or beef chuck","notes":"Poultry or beef carnitas"}]'::jsonb,
