  '"Vegetarian","Gluten-Free","Breakfast","Brunch","Quick Meals","Under 30 mins","Turkish","Middle Eastern","Eggetarian","Nut-Free","High-Protein","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Copper Turkish sahan pan or small skillet","Wooden spatula"',
  '[{"name":"Farm fresh eggs","amount":4,"unit":"large","notes":"Room temperature","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Sweet Turkish green peppers (Sivri or Anaheim), sliced","amount":3,"unit":"peppers","notes":"Mild sweet crunch","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Ripe Roma tomatoes, finely diced","amount":3,"unit":"medium","notes":"Juicy summer tomatoes","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Butter & extra virgin olive oil","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"For cooking vegetables","category":"Dairy"},{"name":"Turkish red pepper flakes (Pul Biber) & oregano","amount":1,"unit":"tsp","notes":"Aromatics","category":"Spices"},{"name":"Crusty artisan bread or simit","amount":1,"unit":"serving","notes":"For dipping","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Sauté Sweet Peppers","instruction":"Melt butter with olive oil in skillet. Add sliced peppers and sauté over medium heat for 4 minutes until softened and sweet.","time":"4 mins","temp":"Medium heat","visualCue":"Tender, bright green peppers."},{"step":2,"title":"Cook Tomatoes to Jammy Sauce","instruction":"Add diced tomatoes, salt, and black pepper. Cook on medium-low for 8 minutes, pressing with spatula until tomatoes melt into a saucy, juicy reduction.","time":"8 mins","temp":"Medium-low heat","visualCue":"Rich red bubbling tomato-pepper stew with released juices."},{"step":3,"title":"Soft-Fold Eggs Gently","instruction":"Lower heat to low. Crack eggs directly into pan. Break yolks with wooden spoon and gently swirl whites through tomato sauce in figure-8 motions. Cook for 2-3 minutes until whites are just set and yolks remain soft and velvety.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Low heat","visualCue":"Soft, custardy yellow and white ribbons running through red sauce."},{"step":4,"title":"Serve Sizzling with Bread","instruction":"Dust with Pul Biber and oregano. Serve straight in the pan with warm bread for communal dipping.","time":"1 min","temp":"Warm","visualCue":"Creamy, juicy scrambled eggs ready to dip."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Never over-scramble the eggs; menemen should be juicy and velvety, not dry like American diner scrambled eggs.","Dipping crusty bread straight into the communal copper pan is the only authentic way to eat menemen."',
  '[{"original":"Green peppers","alternative":"Poblano or green bell pepper","notes":"Mild pepper alternative"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Cooking on high heat until dry","remedy":"Keep heat on low when adding eggs; residual heat will finish setting them."}]'::jsonb,
