  '"Vegetarian","Vegan","Gluten-Free","Dairy-Free","Soup","Comfort Food","American","Quick Meals","Nut-Free","Low-Sugar"',
  '"Baking sheet","High-speed blender or immersion blender","Soup pot"',
  '[{"name":"Butternut squash, peeled, seeded & cubed","amount":800,"unit":"g","notes":"1-inch cubes","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Honeycrisp apple, peeled & diced","amount":1,"unit":"apple","notes":"Natural sweet acidity","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Full-fat coconut milk","amount":1,"unit":"cup","notes":"Silky richness","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Vegetable broth","amount":3,"unit":"cups","notes":"Savory base","category":"Pantry"},{"name":"Fresh ginger & garlic cloves","amount":2,"unit":"tbsp","notes":"Roasted with squash","category":"Produce"},{"name":"Toasted pumpkin seeds (pepitas)","amount":0.25,"unit":"cup","notes":"Crunchy topping","category":"Pantry"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"step":1,"title":"Roast Squash & Aromatics","instruction":"Toss squash cubes, diced apple, garlic cloves, and sliced ginger with olive oil, salt, and nutmeg. Roast at 400°F (200°C) for 25 minutes until caramelized and fork-tender.","time":"25 mins","temp":"400°F (200°C)","visualCue":"Golden brown caramelized edges on sweet squash."},{"step":2,"title":"Puree with Broth & Coconut Milk","instruction":"Transfer warm roasted squash to blender. Add vegetable broth and coconut milk. Blend on high for 90 seconds until ultra-smooth and velvety.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Warm","visualCue":"Lustrous, glowing velvet orange soup."},{"step":3,"title":"Warm & Season","instruction":"Pour soup into pot, bring to a gentle simmer, and season with sea salt and cracked black pepper.","time":"3 mins","temp":"Low simmer","visualCue":"Thick, soothing soup coating the ladle."},{"step":4,"title":"Garnish Swirl & Crunch","instruction":"Ladle into warm bowls. Swirl coconut cream, scatter toasted pepitas, and drizzle hot chili oil.","time":"2 mins","temp":"Warm","visualCue":"White cream swirls and crunchy green pepitas on golden soup."}]'::jsonb,
  '"Roasting the squash first caramelizes its natural fructose, giving a much deeper sweetness than merely boiling it in broth.","The tart sweet apple provides balance so the squash doesn't taste flat."',
  '[{"original":"Coconut milk","alternative":"Heavy dairy cream or cashew cream","notes":"Dairy or nut alternative"}]'::jsonb,
  '[{"mistake":"Using unroasted raw squash","remedy":"Always roast in the oven first for caramelized depth."}]'::jsonb,
  '{}',
  'Vent blender lid when pureeing hot soup to prevent steam pressure buildup.',
  'Freezes for up to 3 months; keeps 5 days in fridge.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1476718406336-bb5a9690ee2a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80',
